                subject: "Derive the update feed repository at build time instead of hardcoding it",
                details: "114 published installers carry \"Ding-Ding-Projects/material-bluemap\" welded\ninto main/index.ts as a string literal, so the moment this project's home\ngets renamed for Worldlens, every one of them keeps knocking on the old\naddress forever - GitHub's rename redirect is a courtesy, not a promise, and\nlapses, name reuse, or a second transfer all break it for good. build.mjs now\nresolves the repository once at bundle time (an explicit\nMATERIAL_BLUEMAP_BUILD_REPOSITORY override, else CI's own GITHUB_REPOSITORY,\nelse a real local-dev fallback) and bakes it into the bundle with esbuild's\n`define`, so main/index.ts never writes the name down again. Inside CI, a\nmissing or malformed GITHUB_REPOSITORY now fails the build loudly instead of\nshipping a guess - because a wrong value here is invisible until updates\nsilently stop arriving, which is the one failure mode worse than a red\nbuild. MATERIAL_BLUEMAP_UPDATE_FEED, the runtime override, is untouched and\nstill wins over whatever got baked in, which is exactly the escape hatch the\nrename will lean on for the 114 installers already out there.\n\n114個裝好嘅安裝包全部都焼死一條寫死嘅repo路徑,呢個project一改名佢哋就企喺原\n地拍緊舊道門,得閒等GitHub幫手轉發——呢個係人情,唔係保證,一失效、一畀人攞返\n嚟用、或者repo再搬多次屋,道門就永遠打唔開。而家build.mjs開工嗰陣先攞一次\n真正嘅repository(自己講明用邊個、唔係就攞CI嘅GITHUB_REPOSITORY、真係乜都無\n先落返個本地開發嘅正版後備),再用esbuild嘅`define`焼入個bundle度,main/\nindex.ts以後唔使再寫死個名。CI入面攞唔到或者格式錯,而家會即刻炸咗畀你睇,\n唔會靜雞雞焼錯個地址落去出貨——因為呢種錯係要等到更新靜靜雞唔再嚟先會發現,\n仲衰過個build直接變紅。MATERIAL_BLUEMAP_UPDATE_FEED呢條後路完全冇郁過,照樣\n贏晒任何焼入去嘅值,改名嗰陣就係靠佢救返出面嗰114個裝好嘅安裝包。",
