                details: "mapStorage.ts's PRODUCT_DIRECTORY carried a comment claiming \"Material\nBlueMap\" (electron-builder's productName) \"is also the leaf of its\nuserData directory\". It never was: this app never calls\napp.setName(), so Electron reads userData's name from package.json's\nraw \"name\" field instead - @material-bluemap/app - and joins the \"/\"\nas a second folder. The setup wizard's fallback default therefore\nshowed %APPDATA%\\Material BlueMap\\maps, a folder beside nothing real,\nwhile the actual userData directory holding consent, the first-run\nflag, the GitHub credential, project history and cached maps sits at\n%APPDATA%\\@material-bluemap\\app. Fixed on Windows only - macOS and\nLinux get no real desktop build, so PRODUCT_DIRECTORY stays there as\nwhat it always was, a display-name guess. Left the obvious \"finish the\njob\" out of scope on purpose, in a comment: calling app.setName() now\nwould rename every existing profile's folder out from under itself\nwith nothing to migrate the old one's contents, so that stays a\nseparate, later change.\n\nPRODUCT_DIRECTORY 嗰個 comment 一直吹水話自己係 userData 個真名,其实\n从来都唔係:呢個app 从来冇call过 app.setName(),Electron 揾嘅係\npackage.json 度个原装 \"@material-bluemap/app\",条 \"/\" 重会拆多層資料夾。\n结果 setup 精灵个默认位一直讲大话,话响 %APPDATA%\\Material BlueMap,\n但真正装晒 consent、GitHub帐号、project history 嘅地方响\n%APPDATA%\\@material-bluemap\\app 度。净係修好 Windows 嗰边(mac/linux\n根本冇真身desktop build),仲留低个comment話明唔好自把自为call\napp.setName() - 咁做会即刻搬冧成个用户嘅旧profile,冇迁移就即刻死人塌屋。",
