                subject: "Put the GitHub CLI on the release job's PATH",
                details: "The release job calls gh nine times - checking the tag is free, counting\nexisting releases for the code-name ordinal, creating the release, uploading\nits assets - and GitHub's hosted image ships the CLI already. This machine does\nnot.\n\nThe symptom was worse than a missing tool usually is. `if gh release view` fails\nsilently, because a failing condition is not an error under set -e, so the tag\ncheck appears to pass. Then `count=$(gh release list ...)` fails the same way\nand, being a command substitution, takes the whole step down with exit 127 - a\ncode that reads like a missing file. Half the step seemed to work on its way to\nan error that named nothing.\n\nFetched into a job-local directory rather than installed with apt, mirroring\nthe shellcheck step in the workflows job: nothing here needs to persist on the\nmachine or be administered, and a runner that already has gh pays nothing.\n\nThis job had never run before tonight - it is gated behind every other job\npassing, and something else had always failed first.\n\n呢個 job 用咗九次 gh,GitHub 部機本身有,呢部冇。仲衰過普通「搵唔到指令」:\n`if gh release view` 失敗唔會當錯,所以個 tag 檢查睇落好似過咗;跟住\n`count=$(gh release list ...)` 一炸,因為係命令替換,成步嘢帶住 127 一齊死——\n127 睇落似搵唔到檔案。即係半步嘢扮到好似做緊嘢,最後畀你一個乜都冇講嘅錯誤碼。\n今次係佢有史以來第一次真係行到,因為前面永遠有第二樣嘢先死。",
