                subject: "Give App.test.ts its own 60s timeout, measured rather than doubled",
                details: "Two of App.test.ts's 34 tests (\"the notification corner\" mounting once,\nand showing a message raised while nothing is open) were hitting the\nworkspace's 30s default in CI - not because App.vue got slower to\nstart, but because this project's self-hosted CI runner was busy.\nMeasured, not assumed: CI run 31074156612 timed both tests out at\n43561ms and 36517ms, and the whole file took 146739ms there against a\nclean 44.37s alone on a dev machine - a ~3.3x slowdown that also shows\nup in ProjectEditor.test.ts (119199ms in CI vs 27.99s locally, running\nconcurrently with this file in the other of vitest.config.ts's two\npinned forks) and in a vue-tsc-shelling typecheck test that spent 54s\nin the same run. App.vue's own mount path was audited for eager work\nand found none: every bridge resolves to null with nothing mounted,\nand the shell mounts in under a second and a half locally whether run\nalone or early inside the full 9,329-test suite. So this gives the\nfile a deliberate, evidence-based 60s ceiling via vi.setConfig instead\nof quietly doubling the workspace default, with the measurements\nrecorded in a comment so the next person does not have to redo this.\n\n冇錯,APP.VUE 冇偷懶,係果部自己搭嘅 CI 機肺活量唔夠,唔係佢自己肥咗先行得\n咁慢。呢個小小嘅殼(成個 shell)本身就係全個 jsdom 套件入面最重嘅嘢,喺\n自己部機度跑,乜都係一秒有多啲,問題係嗰部 CI 機淨係得兩條 fork 頂成\n9,329 條測試,隔籬個 ProjectEditor.test.ts 都係慢咗成四倍,連 vue-tsc\n都嚟湊熱鬧,梗係迫親呢兩條。查完 App.vue 個 mount 路徑,乜嘢都冇偷偷摸摸\n去掃磁碟、探依賴,個 bridge 一係冇一係即刻返 null,所以唔關佢事——淨係\n畀返呢個檔案自己嘅 60 秒上限,仲寫低晒啲數字,慳返下一個人再查一次。",
