                subject: "CI: stop reinstalling Playwright's apt deps on every single run",
                details: "install-deps used to shell out to apt-get, with sudo, unconditionally,\nevery push, forever - fine on a disposable hosted VM, a real and\ngrowing tax on a self-hosted machine that remembers what it installed\nfive minutes ago. Playwright already ships the fix for this and nobody\nwas using it: `install-deps --dry-run` touches nothing, simulates the\napt install against whatever package list the CURRENT Playwright\nversion actually needs, and exits non-zero the moment one thing is\nmissing. Because that list is recomputed live instead of copied into\nthis file once, a future Playwright bump that wants one more library\nstill gets caught correctly - it just no longer costs a full apt-get\nupdate on the 364 runs out of 365 that needed nothing at all.\n\n`install-deps` 呢個嘢以前係唔理三七廿一,每次 push 都幫你落足網去\napt-get 裝一次,喺即用即棄嘅雲端機度冇所謂,但喺自己部機度就即係\n你自己嘅機日日俾人重複裝返啱啱先裝過嘅嘢。原來 Playwright 自己一早\n有解:`install-deps --dry-run` 咩都唔會郁,淨係扮吓依家呢個\nPlaywright 版本需要啲乜,搵到唔夠先至話畀你知。呢個清單係即時計,\n唔係抄一次擺喺度,所以第日 Playwright 升級要多樣嘢,佢照樣捉到,\n唔會靜雞雞漏檢。",
