                date: "2026-08-06T00:41:26-04:00",
                subject: "Warn once when a render-mask list exceeds the cloud renderer's one-box limit",
                details: "Two ordinary, non-subtracting boxes is the single most likely way a drawn\nrender-mask exceeds what the cloud/Actions render path (packages/cli/src/maps.ts\nmaskFor) can translate, and until now nothing on screen said so: the per-shape\nwarning in MaskDrawingCanvas.vue only ever asks \"would this shape alone\ntranslate?\", which is true for each box individually, so it stayed silent while\nthe cloud path quietly rendered the whole world, unmasked. ConfigMaskField.vue\nnow runs a new list-level check, cloudFidelityForMask in maskCanvas.ts, once for\nthe whole top-level mask (never for a blur's own nested list), mirroring\napp/src/main/render/maskFidelity.ts's checkCloudFidelity by hand the same way\nthat file already mirrors maskFor -- same test cases on both sides, so a missed\nhand-sync goes red instead of drifting quietly. New catalogue entries\n(mask.fidelity.listUnsupported) carry the warning through all three language\nmodes and five funny levels while pinning the facts that matter: whole world,\nunmasked, and the single-non-subtracting-box rule itself, not just a dynamic\nreason string a rewrite could quietly drop.\n\n畫多一個箱形係好平常嘅事，但依家先發現：兩個普通、冇相減嘅箱形，就係最容易踩中雲端/Actions\n算圖路線嗰條「淨係識一個箱」底線嘅方法，之前完全冇警告 -- 逐個形狀睇個個都得，成個列表加埋就唔得，\n於是雲端嗰邊靜雞雞算晒成個世界，冇晒遮罩，用戶乜都唔知。而家 ConfigMaskField.vue 加咗一個\nlist-level 嘅檢查，喺成個遮罩列表嗰層先攞一次，唔會喺 blur 入面嘅巢狀列表度再彈多次，同埋喺五個\n搞笑程度、三種語言模式都照樣講到「成個世界」「冇遮罩」呢啲硬道理,唔會俾個搞笑滑桿唔小心搓走咗。",
                category: "interface",
                areas: ["interface", "docs"],
                files: 6,
