                subject: "Give the typecheck step enough heap to survive its own project",
                details: "The first CI run after moving onto a self-hosted runner died in vue-tsc with\n\"Reached heap limit Allocation failed - JavaScript heap out of memory\", exit\n134. Nothing was wrong with the types: vue-tsc holds the entire ui package's\ntype graph in one process, that package grew a great deal in a single night,\nand a hosted runner had been quietly sizing Node's heap against a machine with\nmore room to spare than this one.\n\nRaised to 6 GB for that one step. Scoped to the step rather than the job, so\nnothing else inherits a ceiling it never asked for, and so the next person to\nread this file learns which command is the greedy one.\n\n搬咗去自己部機行 CI,第一鋪就爆記憶體:vue-tsc 要成個 ui package 嘅型別圖一次過\n擺喺一個 process 度,而嗰個 package 今晚肥咗一大截。以前喺 GitHub 部機度冇事,\n係因為嗰邊本身鬆動啲,唔係因為我哋慳。而家淨係俾呢一步加到 6 GB,唔連累其他步驟,\n順便等下一個睇呢個檔案嘅人一眼睇得出邊個指令最貪食。",
                category: "build",
                areas: ["build"],
                files: 1,
