                subject: "Guard the downloads bridge's worldsource routing with a reachability test",
                details: "worldSourceBridge.test.ts proves the mapping - a source's `kind` becoming\nthe panel's `split` flag - but it stays green if someone reverts\npreload/index.ts's discoverRelease from worldsource:discover back to\ndownload:discover. The mapping is not the wiring, and the wiring was the\nwhole point: route through download:* again and a checksum-list world from\nany public repository goes quietly invisible, exactly as the docs used to\nwarn. Nothing failed when the wiring did.\n\nThis test mocks electron, imports the real preload, reads back the object\nhanded to contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld, and asserts each download method\nlands on its worldsource:* channel - and that listDownloads/onDownloadEvent\ndid NOT wander off download:list/download:event, which is as much the\ncontract as the four that moved. Confirmed it bites: reverting discoverRelease\nto download:discover turns exactly that assertion red, then green on restore.\n\n呢個 test 唔係淨係睇個 mapping 啱唔啱,而係守住成條線真係接住 worldsource。\n之前 worldSourceBridge.test.ts 只證到 kind 變 split;有人手痕改返 download:*,\n啲 test 全部照樣綠燈,但跨 repo、SHA256SUMS 分割嘅世界就靜靜雞消失返。而家\nmock 咗 electron,入返真 preload,逐個 method 查佢打邊條頻道;改錯即刻紅,\n改返即刻綠,試過先講。",
                category: "shell",
                areas: ["shell"],
