                subject: "Wire the live speed dial into the interface and fix a broken build",
                details: "The main-process half of live speed adjustment (RenderOrchestrator.adjustSpeed,\nmain/runtime/speedControl.ts, the render:adjustSpeed IPC channel and the preload\nbridge) landed already; this is the other half nobody had built yet, and the\nhalf that lets a person actually see it. LiveSpeedControl.vue draws the 1-5 dial\nbeside a render that is already going, names the render's own current thread\ncount honestly (an \"automatic default\" or a \"Custom\" number, matching no level,\nnever silently snapped), calls the bridge on a click, and shows the exact facts\nthe main process reported back - what applied immediately, what still only\ntakes effect on the next render - rather than a sentence this component made\nup. Restarting to apply the deferred half is offered as its own button, never\ntriggered on its own. RenderThroughput.vue proves the whole thing is not\ntheatre: a live percent-per-minute rate, computed from a short rolling window\nso dragging a level actually moves the number on screen, honestly labelled as\na rate rather than a tile or chunk count neither this port nor upstream's own\nprogress line has ever carried. Caught one real bug writing its own test: the\nthroughput reading was a `computed()` wrapped around a plain closure variable\nwith nothing reactive in it, so it would have cached its first answer forever\nand never once updated on a mounted screen - exactly the \"value is stored,\nnothing reads it\" failure shape this project keeps finding one layer down.\n\n`WorldBridge.adjustRenderSpeed` is optional on the interface itself, on\npurpose: every existing caller across the package that builds its own fake\nbridge predates this method, and marking it required would have broken three\nfiles for a capability they have no reason to know about. A caller reached\nthrough `resolveWorldBridge` never sees it missing regardless - the wrapper\nalways answers with the same refusal shape a genuinely unsupported build\nwould give.\n\nAlso: `copy/surfaces/index.ts` already imported `./liveSpeed.js` from an\nearlier commit that swept it up mid-write, without the file it was importing\nexisting anywhere in git. HEAD has been building against a module that was\nonly ever on one working tree's disk. This commit is that module, landing\nwhere it should have the first time.\n\n一齊嚟講吓做咗乜嘢:上次個 commit 淨係整咗個「調速」嘅後台,冇整到畀人撳嘅嘢 —\nIPC 通咗,preload 都有咗,但成個 app 入面連一粒撳得郁嘅掣都冇。今次補返嗰皮:\nrender 進行緊嗰陣,旁邊就有個 1 至 5 級嘅掣,老實話你知而家嘅執行緒數量係自動\n定係自訂,撳落去就即刻問返後台「啱啱郁咗乜嘢、乜嘢要等落次先算數」,絕對唔會\n自己作故仔呃你話「即刻生效」。想真係即刻套用晒,就有個獨立嘅「重新啟動」掣,\n唔會未問過你就自把自為幫你重開。仲加咗個即時速率顯示,證明個掣真係郁到嘢\n而唔係得個樣 —— 寫緊個測試嗰陣仲執到一隻真.臭蟲:個顯示用緊嘅 computed() 入面\n淨係讀緊一個普通變數,冇半點反應性,結果會永遠停喺第一個答案度唔郁,即係「個\n掣裝咗,但冇人真係讀緊佢個值」嗰種老屋企病。\n\n仲有:`copy/surfaces/index.ts` 之前已經有個 commit 手多多將佢 import 埋\n`./liveSpeed.js`,但嗰份檔案本身從來冇入過 git —— 即係 HEAD 一直靠住一個\n淨係存在於某條工作樹磁碟度嘅模組先建到出嚟。今次就係補返嗰份檔案,遲到好過\n冇到。",
