                subject: "Let the create-a-map wizard render several dimensions at once",
                details: "DimensionSelection.vue mounts under the identity step's own dimension\npicker and lists every dimension the world has, the primary one\nincluded but disabled with the reason it stays ticked. Its own search\nbar carries the full regex builder (ConfigSearchField/regexEngine,\nthe same pair every other list in this app uses), and bulk include/\nexclude/invert act only on whatever the search is currently showing,\nskipping the primary automatically so \"include everything\" never\nduplicates the map already being built above it.\n\nTicking a dimension no longer means abandoning the wizard to hand-\nedit a project afterwards: wizardModel.ts's toRenderRequest now\nbuilds one extra RenderMapRequest per ticked dimension, each from\nBlueMap's own per-dimension template (so the Nether keeps the\nNether's sky colour rather than the Overworld's), with an id and name\nderived from the primary map's own - survival, survival-the-nether,\nsurvival-the-end - and pointed at a split-server dimension's own\nsibling folder when it has one. None of the primary map's hand-tuned\noption edits are replayed onto an extra map, since a setting tuned\nfor one dimension does not necessarily suit another; every extra map\nstays reachable afterwards through the project editor like any other.\nThe review step now names every extra map that will be created,\nby id and by the folder it renders from, so nothing about the render\nis a surprise by the time the button is pressed.\n\nNether, End and any dimension a mod or datapack added all start\nunticked, on purpose: rendering the Nether is not always wanted, and\nthis app has no way to size an unrecognised custom dimension before\nsomebody asks for it, so the safer default is to ask rather than\nguess. The Overworld renders alone until somebody says otherwise,\nexactly as it always has.\n\nDimensionSelection.vue喺個identity step自己嗰個維度揀選掣下面企定,\n列晒個世界擁有嘅每一個維度,連正名嗰個都有得列,不過剔咗兼disable咗,\n仲講明點解佢一定要剔住。自己嗰個search bar照樣掛住成套regex\nbuilder(ConfigSearchField/regexEngine,同呢個程式其他清單用緊嗰套一\n樣),bulk嘅include/exclude/invert淨係郁動緊喺搜尋緊嗰啲,遇正名嗰個\n自動跳過,所以「全部剔晒」永遠唔會將上面度緊嗰張地圖多整一份出嚟。\n\n剔咗一個維度,唔使再走去hand-edit個project先算數:wizardModel.ts嘅\ntoRenderRequest而家會幫每個剔咗嘅維度整多張RenderMapRequest,全部由\nBlueMap自己嗰個維度範本整出嚟(即係話地獄照樣用返地獄嘅天色,唔會亂\n用Overworld嗰隻),id同名都係跟正名地圖自己嘅嚟-\nsurvival、survival-the-nether、survival-the-end\n-遇正劈開咗嘅伺服器維度,就指去佢自己嗰個親戚資料夾。正名地圖手動改\n過嘅選項唔會照搬去額外嗰啲度,因為一個維度啱嘅設定未必啱second個;\n每張額外地圖之後照樣可以喺project editor度打開嚟改,同其他地圖冇兩\n樣。覆核步驟而家會列晒每一張即將整嘅額外地圖,連id同去邊個資料夾都\n講埋,所以撳掣嗰下之前乜都唔會嚇親你。\n\n地獄、終界,同埋任何mod或者datapack加落去嘅維度,全部預設唔剔,呢個\n係特登嘅:唔係次次都想連地獄一齊算,而呢個程式又冇辦法喺有人問之前\n就知一個唔識嘅自訂維度有幾大,所以穩陣啲嘅做法係問清楚先,唔好亂咁\n估。Overworld就繼續自己一個算,直至有人講第二句為止,同以前一樣。",
                category: "interface",
                areas: ["interface", "docs"],
                files: 10,
