                subject: "Refuse a foreign file at the marker's own path, as the module already promised",
                details: "bootstrap.ts states that a file it did not write is refused rather than\noverwritten, and the two workflow templates genuinely were: isAppOwnedFile\nguards both. The marker itself was not. writeMarker read any existing file for\nits sha and then wrote straight over it, so a stray file that happened to sit\nat .material-bluemap-ci.json was replaced without a word.\n\nThe filename makes that collision vanishingly unlikely, which is exactly the\nargument that lets a hole like this sit in a stated guarantee forever.\n\"Unlikely\" is not \"refused\", and quietly replacing somebody's file is the one\noutcome no amount of unlikeliness excuses. The check keys on authorship, not\nversion, so an older build still updates a marker a newer one wrote - keying on\nversion would have deadlocked the pair against each other.\n\nVerified the way this project verifies a guard: the new test was watched\nfailing against the unfixed code first (1 failed, 13 passed), then passing\nafter (14/14).\n\n個模組自己講明「唔係我寫嘅檔案,一律唔郁」,兩個 workflow 檔案的確做到,偏偏\n負責記錄「邊啲檔案係我寫」嗰個 marker 自己冇人守——見到有嘢就照覆蓋。\n借口係「邊會咁啱有人擺個同名檔案喺度啫」,但呢句正正就係啲窿一世都補唔到嘅原因。\n而家改成睇「係咪我哋寫嘅」而唔係睇版本號,唔係就唔郁;睇版本號嘅話,新舊版本\n會互相唔敢覆蓋,鎖死。",
