                subject: "Show worlds ready to use on the Projects tab, discovered automatically",
                details: "The Projects tab used to start empty until a project existed - even when the\nworld catalogue the wizard already reads from could see worlds sitting right\nthere. A new panel (DiscoveredWorldsPanel.vue) surfaces that same catalogue on\nthe Projects tab itself: automatic on tab open, no click required, background\nscanning that never blocks the page.\n\nReused rather than reimplemented: the main-process discovery and mount\nmachinery (packages/app/src/main/world/{locations,mounts,catalog}.ts, landed\nin the previous commit), the WorldCatalogBridge contract, and every pure\nformatting/sorting/search-text function in worldCatalog.ts - the exact same\npieces the wizard's own MinecraftWorldList.vue calls. Only the presentation is\nnew, because the interaction genuinely differs: the wizard picks one world to\nfill a field, this tab starts projects, potentially several at once, with\nmulti-select and a per-row context menu the wizard's plain listbox never\nneeded.\n\nA discovered world is not silently turned into a project. discoveredWorlds.ts\nfilters the catalogue against the tab's own project list by path identity\n(the same samePath every other match in this codebase uses, folding case and\nseparators), and every row carries a \"not yet a project\" chip and its own\ndashed-border card, distinct from the established list beneath it. One click\nopens the editor pre-filled and unsaved - a one-click route in, never an\nunasked-for write; the bulk action writes several default projects at once\nthrough the same host.writeProject a normal Save already calls.\n\nDe-duplication: worldCatalog.ts gains dedupeWorldsByPath, keying a world by\nits normalised path rather than the object identity a raw list would trust,\nas the defensive second layer beside the existing folder-level dedup in\nmounts.ts. Four honest states are told apart on screen: still scanning, no\nfolder added at all, folders added but empty, and every world already\nclaimed by a project - plus a fifth for a search with no match.\n\nRight-click, its own search field and Shift+right-click straight to the\nappearance editor arrive for free from AppearanceTarget, the same wrapper\nProjectList.vue's own rows already use - no second implementation of any of\nit. Every string routes through vue-i18n with an English fallback, ready for\nCantonese/bilingual voicing once components/project joins the catalogue\ncoverage guard's list, which it does not yet (a pre-existing gap this panel\ninherits rather than creates).\n\nNew docs/project-world-discovery.md, cross-linked with docs/finding-worlds.md\n(itself updated for the Bedrock and CurseForge locations from the previous\ncommit) and indexed in both docs/README.md and the in-app documentation\nbrowser's APPLICATION_ORDER.\n\n475 tests green across packages/ui/src/components/project, .../world and\n.../docs (28 files); vue-tsc and eslint clean on every touched file.\n\nThe Projects 分頁以前淨係得個吉盒,擺明個電腦度有嘢佢都唔講。而家佢會自動彈晒啲搵到嘅\n世界出嚟,仲用返嗰套 wizard 本來就有嘅搵嘢機器,冇整多一套第二個。搵到嘅世界同真係開咗\n嘅 project 分得好清楚,一撳就入編輯器,唔會匿埋幫你偷偷寫嘢落個世界度。",
