                subject: "Unbreak the typecheck the overlay work left behind, and register two menus",
                details: "Two errors of the same species were failing CI: a ternary over array indices\nthat strict index checking cannot narrow, and a pile of vMenuTags(...)[0] in\nthe guard's own detector tests. Neither is a real defect; both are TypeScript\nbeing right about something the surrounding assertions had already proved.\n\nThe test file gets an onlyTag() helper that throws when the sweep did not\nreturn exactly one tag, rather than an assertion that quietly tolerates\nundefined. That distinction matters more here than anywhere: these are the\ntests proving the detector SEES a collision, so an assertion handed undefined\nwould report a detector that found nothing at all as working perfectly.\n\nAlso registered SimpleHistoryList.vue and SimpleHistoryPanel.vue, which the\ninventory half of the guard correctly refused to let ship unnamed. Both use\nactivator=\"parent\" on a small export button with no :target beside it, so they\nare clean, but \"clean\" is a claim the registry has to make out loud.\n\nTypeScript 又贏一鋪:兩處明明前面已經驗過長度,佢照樣話「可能係 undefined」。\n今次冇用驚嘆號硬撳落去,改為寫個 onlyTag() ——搵唔到就即刻嘈,唔會扮冇嘢。\n呢個位尤其緊要:呢啲測試本身就係用嚟證明個偵測器「見到」個問題,如果收到\nundefined 都當冇事,咁一個乜都搵唔到嘅偵測器反而次次滿分。\n另外兩個新歷史面板嘅匯出選單都要入册——佢哋本身係安全寫法,不過「安全」呢句\n係要寫明出嚟,唔係心照。",
