                details: "tabindex=\"-1\" made every registered heading, paragraph, table cell, card and the\nsite footer focusable by script, which is exactly what focus-RETURN after closing\na mouse-opened menu needed -- and exactly why it was useless for getting there in\nthe first place: -1 is defined to sit outside the natural Tab order, so nothing\never tabbed onto one of these elements, so its own ContextMenu/Shift+F10 handler\n(which only fires once the element already has focus) never got a chance to run.\nA keyboard-only visitor could return from a menu they never had any way to open.\n\nFixed with installRovingAppearanceFocus(): the same roving-tabindex idiom the tab\nstrip already uses. Each page's decoratePage() traversal, and the standalone\nfooter, now hand their registered group to it -- exactly one member becomes a\nreal Tab stop, and ArrowDown/Right, ArrowUp/Left, Home and End roving-focus across\nthe rest, so every element in the group is reachable without turning an article\ninto a wall of meaningless Tab stops. Natively focusable elements are left alone.\n\n之前 tabindex=\"-1\" 得個焦點返鄉證,冇通行證:焦點閂咗個選單之後識得飛翔返去掛喺嗰\n度嘅標題度,但正常人由頭行到嗰度嘅路,壓根就冇起過。Tab键行到嗰個標題面前,直情\n飄過去,乜都冇留低,梗係唔知入面仲有個ContextMenu快捷键喺度等緊。而家跟返個分頁\n攞用開嗰招\"輪流坐莊\"式tabindex:一組入面揀一個做正式停靠站,再用方向键、Home、\nEnd輪流飞去第二個,keyboard-only嘅訪客先至真係入到門。\n\nTests: 5 new assertions in contextMenu.test.ts under\n\"installRovingAppearanceFocus gives a registered group a real keyboard entry\npoint\" -- watched all 5 go red with the function neutralized to a no-op before\nrestoring the real implementation and confirming green (14/14 in the file).",
