                subject: "Land first-run setup on Home, not the wizard; make its guard test real",
                details: "First-run setup's onFirstRunFinished() called revealPage(PAGE_WORLD) directly,\nso the instant a brand-new install finished the welcome/licence/consent/storage\nflow, the active tab became the wizard and Home - the screen built to answer\n\"where do I start\" - was skipped every single time, reachable only by noticing\nits pinned, icon-only tab. It now calls revealPage(PAGE_HOME) instead; Home's\nown hero card is \"Make a map\" (weighted primary), so the wizard stays exactly\none click away. Returning users are unaffected: the handler only ever fires\nonce, on a genuine first-time completion, so a persisted workspace's last\nactive tab is never touched.\n\nThe test titled \"opens on Home for a fresh install\" passed while asserting\nnothing of the sort: it mounted a freshly-seeded workspace in isolation and\nnever drove FirstRunSetup's own completion event, so it would have kept\npassing green throughout the whole life of this bug. It's split in two now -\none test proving the bare seed defaults to Home, and one that emits the real\n`finished` event and checks Home landed - plus a new companion test proving a\nreturning user's saved workspace is left alone. Watched both new tests go red\nagainst the reverted revealPage(PAGE_WORLD) body first (\"expected false to be\ntrue\" / \"expected 'false' to be 'true'\" on the Home checks) before restoring\nthe fix, so the guard is proven rather than assumed.\n\nHome's docs article gains a section on where first-run setup actually lands,\nand a written exemption for why its capability grid - a fixed catalogue of\ndestinations, not user records - is deliberately outside the project's\nbulk-actions rule.\n\n一開波個精靈就將人直接掟去「開世界」個分頁，Home 呢版特登整嚟答「應該去邊」嘅，\n就咁畀佢當透明。仲有條測試成日話自己揸緊住個 Home 唔畀走數，其實佢自己都冇揸過\n嗰條真係完成安裝先觸發嘅路，淨係開個假工作區就當交足貨——而家改咗做真係掟去\nHome，個測試都改到係真係揸住嗰條路先算，重加埋一條保住老用戶原本嗰個分頁唔會\n被拉返去 Home。",
