                subject: "Re-index 9 shipped docs articles into the in-app docs browser's categories",
                details: "docs/README.md's \"The application\" and \"Rendering\" tables have listed\nhome.md, path-field.md, dependency-provisioning.md,\njava-runtime-provisioning.md, scheduled-render.md, ssh-world-sources.md,\ndocker-world-source.md, world-git-repository.md and remote-hosting.md for a\nwhile now. docsModel.ts's APPLICATION_ORDER / RENDERING_ORDER arrays never\nheard about any of them - each shipped in its own feature commit, and each\none forgot the one line that tells the bundled docs browser which heading it\nsits under. The article content itself was never lost or unreachable; it\njust fell into the \"uncategorized\" bucket instead of grouping under \"The\napplication\" or \"Rendering\" the way its neighbours do, quietly drifting from\nthe hand-maintained index it is supposed to mirror. Nine separate commits,\nnine separate forgetful moments, now fixed in the one place that reads them.\n\ndocs/README.md 個「應用程式」同「渲染」表格,老早就寫低咗呢九篇文,\ndocsModel.ts 嗰兩個排序陣列就一直冇收到風,梗係啦,冇一個功能commit係專登\n嚟改呢一行嘅。篇文本身冇不見,淨係跌咗落「未分類」個桶,冇同佢啲兄弟姊妹企埋\n一齊。九個commit,九次唔記得,而家一次過幫佢哋認返祖歸宗。",
