                subject: "Wire a Home tab: every capability in one place, opening menus not just tabs",
                details: "Eight unexplained tabs used to be the first thing a brand-new install showed,\nbefore the first-run dialog even finished asking its own questions. Home is\nthe answer: one pinned landing tab, first in the strip, that names every\ncapability this app has - weighted so a newcomer sees the single obvious next\nstep (Make a map) and a returning user sees what they were doing last\n(Continue). Every card's action reuses the exact verb the command palette\nalready calls for the same destination - reveal-page, open-settings at an\nanchor, app.appState.menu.openPage - so clicking a tile opens the actual menu\nat the actual decision, not merely a screen with more hunting to do. Backups\nand Publish to Pages say plainly when there is no rendered map yet and offer\nthe one button that fixes it, rather than a control that would fail the\nmoment it was pressed. The intro remembers being collapsed; the search bar\ncarries the project's own regex builder; every region is a real appearance\ntarget. The existing tab strip - overflow, reordering, pinning, grouping, its\nfour searches, its persistence - is untouched: Home is additive, riding the\npinned-page-ids/ensurePage primitives already built for exactly this landing\npage, so both a fresh install and an upgrading one get it without losing\ntheir place.\n\n八個冇解釋過嘅分頁，以前係一部新裝機第一眼見到嘅嘢，仲要早過首次執行嘅對話\n框問完自己嗰堆問題。Home 就係答案：一個釘死喺分頁列最前面嘅主頁，將呢個程式\n識做嘅嘢全部擺晒出嚟 - 排位方面，新手見到嘅係最應該做嗰步（整張地圖），老用\n戶見到嘅係佢上次做緊嘅嘢（繼續）。每張卡嘅動作，用嘅係指令面板去開同一個去\n處嗰個一模一樣嘅動詞 - reveal-page、帶錨點嘅 open-settings、\napp.appState.menu.openPage - 所以撳一張卡開嘅係嗰個決定本身嘅選單，唔係一個\n仲要再搵嘢嘅畫面。備份同發佈去 Pages 會老實講仲未有算好嘅地圖，仲會俾返嗰粒\n真係解決到問題嘅掣，而唔係一個一撳就死嘅控制項。簡介記得自己收埋咗未；搜尋\n欄帶埋成個專案自己嗰套 regex 產生器；每一個區域都係真外觀目標。原本嗰個分\n頁列 - 溢出、重新排序、釘住、分組、四個搜尋、記憶 - 全部冇郁過：Home 係加落\n去嘅，攤正正正搭住早排已經整定、專登俾呢個主頁用嘅 pinned-page-ids/\nensurePage 呢兩件嘢，所以新裝機同升級緊嘅機都攞得到，唔會整走佢哋本身企緊\n嗰度。",
