                subject: "Build the one-button winget/Chocolatey installer panel",
                details: "DependencyInstallerPanel.vue is the surface the user asked for: one button\nthat installs every missing dependency, with the route (winget/Chocolatey),\nsize and administrator-permission disclosure shown before it is pressed -\nnever as a mid-install surprise. Per-row progress renders exactly what the\npackage manager reported: Chocolatey's real percentages as a determinate\nbar, winget's phase-only stdout as an honest indeterminate one, nothing\nfabricated either way. A failed row shows its real exit code and message. A\nCancel button reports honestly what finished and what did not.\n\nGets the shared contract largely for free by reusing what already exists\nrather than reinventing it: ConfigSearchField for the anchored regex-builder\nsearch bar, AppearanceTarget for the per-row context menu (own search,\ndisplayed shortcuts, Shift+right-click straight to the appearance editor),\nand raiseNotice() for non-blocking notifications retained in the centre.\nBulk selection (all/invert/none, an honest count of rows that would actually\nchange) and an exportable install log (JSON/Markdown/plain text) are new\nhere, matching the shape ProjectList.vue's own bulk toolbar already uses.\n\ndependencyBridge.ts is a new, separate bridge file rather than an addition\nto the shared settingsBridge.ts, which is mid-edit for the Java-provisioning\nconsent flow elsewhere in this same task cycle - same reasoning as keeping\nthe sysdeps main-process engine in its own directory.\n\n裝嘢嗰粒掣造好晒：撳落去之前就話晒俾你知邊個用邊條路裝、使唔使Windows問你攞\n權限，唔會裝到一半先嚇你一跳。真係幾多個巴仙就畫幾多個巴仙，唔識嘅嘢老老實\n實畫個唔知道嘅轉圈仔，唔會呃你話「就嚟得㗎喇」。",
