                subject: "Wire Java provisioning behind explicit consent, not just discovery",
                details: "allowProvisioning has defaulted to false everywhere ensureJava is called, so the\ndownload/verify/extract pipeline in java/provision.ts was reachable from nothing a user\ncould click, even though the failure copy on screen already promised \"the app can fetch\none for you.\" This adds the missing plumbing: a java/consent.ts record (same shape as\nthe Mojang EULA consent, asked once, remembered forever) plus three new IPC channels\n(java:downloadConsent, java:acceptDownloadConsent, java:provision) that gate a real\ndownload on that consent and stream ProvisionEvent progress to every window. The UI\nwiring that turns this into a button follows in the next commit.\n\nJava 一直得個講字冇個做字：允許下載嗰個開關全部程式入面預設係關嗮，settings 個畫面仲吹到明明可以\n幫手落載，但成個掣都冇。呢次補返條路：一個下載同意記錄（照抄 Mojang EULA 嗰個做法，問一次記一世），\n加三條 IPC 頻道畀主程式同意先至肯落載，同一路播返個進度出嚟。畫面上嗰粒掣，下個 commit 先至加。",
