                subject: "Exempt the remote file browser's own path field from the local-dialog guard",
                details: "The path-field policy guard's structural sweep correctly caught a new\nfield: RemoteFileBrowser.vue's address-bar input, added with the SSH\nfile browser, had no PathField.vue browse button and no exemption. The\nguard was right to flag it - it is genuinely path-shaped - but wiring\nPathField.vue to it would be the wrong fix: that control opens a LOCAL\nElectron folder dialog, which would let a user browse this machine's\nown filesystem while looking at a remote host's directory listing.\n\nThis project already made that exact call once, for RemoteTargetEditor\n.vue's workDir field, and recorded the reasoning under the \"remote-\nmachine\" exemption category. The address-bar field sits inside that\nsame reasoning's better half: it is the file browser's own input,\nalready synchronised bidirectionally with the breadcrumb and grid it\nrenders beside, and it is literally the dialog that workDir's own\n\"Browse...\" button opens. It carries the remote equivalent of a browse\naffordance already; PathField.vue would only browse the wrong machine.\n\nAdded one PATH_FIELD_EXEMPTIONS entry, following the existing workDir\nentry's shape and reasoning rather than inventing a new pattern. All 9\npathFieldPolicy tests pass, plus the 171 tests across every file in\ncomponents/remote and the 28 in the main-process browse.ts suite;\nvue-tsc and eslint are clean on the touched file.\n\n呢個guard唔係壞咗,佢係捉到真嘢:新出嘅SSH file browser自己個地址欄,\n冇個browse掣,又冇話明點解冇。直接綁PathField.vue就大鑊喇 - 嗰個掣係\n喺呢部機度開返個local資料夾揀選視窗,睇緊個遠端資料夾就同你講揀返你\n自己部機嘅嘢,答非所問。呢個位之前已經拆解過一次:RemoteTargetEditor\n.vue嘅workDir field都係用\"remote-machine\"呢個豁免原因,而家個address\nbar本身就係workDir個\"Browse...\"掣開嗰個browser,同breadcrumb同格仔\n表雙向同步緊,所以佢自己已經有得\"browse\"喇,唔使再拷貝多次個local\n揀選器落嚟班門弄斧。跟返個舊例加一條豁免,冇縮短張清單,冇放寬掃描。",
                category: "interface",
                areas: ["interface"],
