                details: "ReleaseDownloader.options.concurrency was a plain number read once when the\ndownloader was built, so a Settings control writing a new value would never\nchange a running app's behaviour - the same trap render memory's jvmArgs\nwas in before it took a function. concurrency now accepts a number or a\n() => number, resolved once per download() call rather than at\nconstruction, and DownloadRequest gains its own optional concurrency that\nalways wins over the configured default, mirroring RenderRequest.jvmArgs\nexactly. WorldSourceFetcher shares the same options type and had the\nidentical bug in its own transfer loop; fixed the same way. New tests prove\nthe configured number actually caps how many part requests are in flight at\nonce (not just that it renders or parses), that it re-reads on every\ndownload rather than freezing at construction, and that a per-request\noverride wins.\n\n以前个 concurrency 一开 downloader 就定咗形，Settings 度点写新数字都系做戏，\n同 render 个 heap 上限之前中嗰招一模一样。而家改到每次 download() 先至读，\n仲俾单次要求自己嘅数字赢过设定，同 jvmArgs 嗰套一样。WorldSourceFetcher\n用紧同一份 options，一齐执埋。新测试证明返个数字真系限住咗几多个 part\n同时喺度攞紧，唔系净系画面度靓仔。",
