                subject: "Fix CI typecheck: narrow the remote hosting test mocks to their real union arms",
                details: "The mocks for startRemoteHosting/stopRemoteHosting returned object literals\nwith a plain `ok: true`, which TypeScript widens to `boolean` the moment it\ncrosses vi.fn()'s own generic inference - so neither ever matched the\ndiscriminated `RemoteHostResult`/`RemoteHostStopResult` union in\nhosting.ts/hostingBridge.ts, both keyed on the literal `ok: true`. `as const`\non each literal keeps the type exactly `true`, satisfying the real contract\nwith no cast and no loosening of the production types.\n\nWhile in the file: every mock only ever answered success, so nothing here\nhad actually exercised what the panel does when a publish or a stop is\nrefused - it reads `result.failure.message` into a real error alert on both\npaths. Added one test per path driving the `ok: false` arm, the stop-hosting\none calling the component's own exposed `removeHosting()` directly since\nfully redriving the two-key super-confirmation slider belongs to the test\nthat already covers the gate, not to this one.\n\n呢個 mock 一直呃緊 TypeScript：話自己係 `RemoteHostResult`，其實得返\n`{ ok: boolean }`咁闊,同真正嗰個判別式 union 對唔上,所以 CI 一路紅哂。\n加返 `as const` 就即刻執翻正,一個字都冇改production嗰邊嘅型。仲有,原本啲\nmock 由頭到尾得返成功嗰面,失敗嗰條路一直冇人行过 - 而家幫publish同stop\n都各加一個测试,行返 `ok: false` 嗰邊,证明個panel真係識读错误讯息出嚟畀\n用户睇,唔係得个靓样冇料到。",
