                subject: "Fix the Docker world source's overclaimed test count, false no-override claim, and unwired change check",
                details: "Three defects a review of the new Docker/SSH/git world-source lanes\nfound, all fixed against the current tree rather than assumed:\n\n- docs/ssh-world-sources.md claimed 85 tests for\n  remote/worldsource.ts + windowsShell.ts + worldsource/sshFetcher.ts\n  + sshIpc.ts; the real, currently-passing count is 64 (35+8+4+17).\n  Corrected to the number vitest actually reports.\n- \"The one refusal that has no override\" was false: fetch() takes an\n  explicit acknowledgeLiveRisk flag that overrides the running-container\n  refusal, and failure.ts's own message names it as a third option\n  alongside stopping the server or using a backup. Retitled the section\n  and rewrote failure.ts's comment, docker-world-source.md and\n  docs/README.md to say what is actually true: the refusal has no\n  *standing* override - no setting, no default-true flag - only a\n  fresh, explicit, per-call acknowledgement.\n- dockerWorldFingerprint/fingerprintsEqual (dockerworld/change.ts) had\n  no caller anywhere. Added DockerWorldFetcher.fingerprint(), and\n  exposed it plus fingerprintsEqual over two new IPC channels\n  (dockerworld:fingerprint, dockerworld:fingerprintsEqual), matching\n  exactly how worldrepo:remoteTip and worldsource:ssh:survey/diff\n  expose theirs. Verified render-world.yml's world-source choices are\n  repository/url/release-asset/git only and evaluateScheduleChange has\n  no \"docker\" comparator - a GitHub-hosted Actions runner has no route\n  to a local Docker daemon, the same structural reason the SSH route's\n  own survey/diff was never wired into that GitHub Actions lane either.\n  Documented that boundary explicitly instead of leaving the capability\n  reachable by nobody.\n\n執嗰次新開嘅 Docker/SSH/git 世界來源三條產線審查揪出嚟嘅三隻蟲，\n逐隻對住而家棵樹核實先至郁手，唔係靠估：\n\n- docs/ssh-world-sources.md 寫住 85 個測試，其實跑出嚟得 64 個\n  （35+8+4+17）——文件同現實對唔上數，即刻改番用 vitest 話畀你聽嘅真數。\n- 「呢個拒絕冇得覆蓋」呢句係唔啱嘅：fetch() 本身就收\n  acknowledgeLiveRisk 呢支旗，畀你明刀明槍蓋過個拒絕，連 failure.ts\n  自己嗰句提示都話咗呢個係第三條路。改咗個標題，重寫\n  failure.ts、docker-world-source.md 同 docs/README.md，講返啱嘅嘢：\n  冇嘅係「長期覆蓋」——冇設定、冇預設開嘅旗；每次都要新鮮、\n  明確咁確認先算。\n- dockerWorldFingerprint/fingerprintsEqual（dockerworld/change.ts）\n  一直得個講字，冇人用過。加咗 DockerWorldFetcher.fingerprint()，再開\n  多兩條 IPC 頻道（dockerworld:fingerprint、\n  dockerworld:fingerprintsEqual）攞出嚟，同 worldrepo:remoteTip 同\n  worldsource:ssh:survey/diff 一模一樣做法。核實過\n  render-world.yml 嘅 world-source 得返\n  repository/url/release-asset/git，evaluateScheduleChange 都冇\n  \"docker\" 呢隻比較器——GitHub 嘅雲端 runner 本身就去唔到你部機嘅\n  Docker daemon，同 SSH 嗰邊嘅 survey/diff 一直冇入到嗰條排程算染\n  防線係一模一樣嘅結構性原因。呢個界線寫清楚咗，唔留低一個得把口冇人用嘅功能。",
