                subject: "Gate release on the real Java config round-trip, fix stale CI comment",
                details: "The config-java-roundtrip job proved itself on hosted runners today but was\nnever added to the release job's needs, so a release could still ship a\nconfig writer that fails to round-trip a value into the real upstream CLI's\nsettings.json - exactly the defect a user would hit the instant they saved a\nsetting. It is now a hard gate. The added cost is close to nothing: the job\nneeds only `jars` and finishes in under a minute once that is ready (28s\nobserved end to end), while release already waits on check, package and\ntest-world, each of which takes several minutes on its own - so the new gate\nis never the slowest thing release is blocked on, it is just an extra promise\nkept before publishing.\n\nAlso corrected e2e.test.ts's own doc comment, which still said the \"Lint,\nbuild, test\" job checks the repository out without the vendor/BlueMap\nsubmodule. That stopped being true earlier today once submodules: true and\nMBM_VENDOR_REQUIRED=1 were wired onto that job, so the webapp-bundle scenario\nthis comment was explaining now actually runs in CI instead of recording a\nskip every time - the comment was describing a CI that no longer exists.\n\n放閘總好過返工先驚:config-java-roundtrip 呢個job今日先至喺runner度真係走得,\n但冇人叫佢睇住個release閘,即係話個config writer就算真係寫壞咗都可以照樣出街,\n到用戶手多多save一個setting就即刻中招。而家實牙實齒foreach佢入去,\n成本平到笑:jars一得手佢就28秒搞掂,release本身要等嘅嗰幾個job個個都行幾分鐘,\n所以呢道新閘從來未做過\"拖慢晒\"嗰個角色。順手執返e2e.test.ts個註釋,\n佢仲喺度講vendor submodule冇check out添——今日已經改咗,個comment講緊嘅\nalready係舊聞。",
