                subject: "CI: actually run the real Java CLI round-trip test, not skip it",
                details: "javaRoundTrip.test.ts proves the whole point of the HOCON reader/writer by\nhanding an edited config folder to the real upstream CLI jar and checking\nits own settings.json agrees - but it was gated on a jar and a JVM that\nthis workflow never supplied, so every hosted run quietly filed it as\n\"skipped, not failed\" and called that a passing suite. A test that only\never runs on someone's laptop is a rumour with a green checkmark.\n\nAdd a `config-java-roundtrip` job that needs only `jars` (not `check`, to\navoid serialising the fast lint/build/test loop behind a full upstream\nGradle build), downloads the `bluemap-jar-cli` artifact that job already\nproduces, sets up JDK 25 to match upstream's pinned toolchain, and points\nBLUEMAP_CLI_JAR at the downloaded jar so the test's own skipIf gate opens\nfor real.\n\nCI 而家真係走一次 javaRoundTrip.test.ts,唔再淨係喺自己部電腦度「通過」。\n呢個測試專登用返 upstream 嘅真.jar 去驗證 HOCON reader/writer 讀寫嘅嘢啱唔啱,\n但之前個 workflow 從來冇俾過佢 jar 同 JVM,所以每次跑 CI 都靜靜雞畀佢 skip\n咗,個綠剔完全冇證明過乜嘢。而家加咗個新 job,淨係靠 `jars`(唔搭埋\n`check`,唔想成條 pipeline 等成個 Gradle build 先郁得),攞返個 CLI jar,\n裝返 JDK 25,set 好 BLUEMAP_CLI_JAR,等個測試真係郁手做嘢,唔係得個講字。",
