                details: "Ground truth this session closed both of these features' exit criteria for\nreal: issue #31 (textures.json semantic parity for vanilla and a modded\npack, live blockstate resolution, a real 1.12.2 jar through the legacy\npath with its own bug found and fixed as #46) and issue #44 (a real\ndesktop publish against a throwaway public repository, its private-repo\nfailure path, and an 839MB/20,632-file publish, all independently\nre-verified live). Both articles said \"ported\" past the point where that\nwas still true; they now say \"shipped\" and name what each run actually\nproved.\n\nAlso corrected three articles a new guard test caught drifting out from\nunder the same ground truth: viewer-remote-mode and config-rich-controls\nstill asserted the java-render-path and options-gui exit checks \"had not\nrun\" after this session proved otherwise elsewhere on the site, and\ninstall still said the local render path \"has not run in CI\" after a\nreal Java-engine render started running in CI on every push. A\nrelease-pipeline suggestion line calling resource-packs an example of\nopen exit criteria was reworded to match.\n\nhome.ts: promoted its resource-packs card, and brought the phase table's\nPhase C and Phase D rows and the two-engines section back in line with\nROADMAP.md, which already recorded both as done (the D gate closed on\n2026-08-04, C's exit criteria closed on 2026-08-05) while the site's own\nmirror still called them in-progress with stale \"has not run\" notes.\nPhase F's note now says the options-gui exit check has run rather than\nhas not.\n\nNew guard in content.test.ts, in two parts: one confirms every status\nvalue used by an article or a home-page feature card is one the i18n\ncatalogue and the renderer's STATUS_LABEL_KEYS actually know how to\nbadge; the other bans a shipped article's own words from asserting its\nexit check \"has not run\" at all. The second one is deliberately narrow\naround whole-feature \"never ran\" phrases rather than short words like\n\"unproven\", because this codebase's house style keeps writing real,\ndisclosed residual gaps into shipped articles under headings like \"What\nhas not been checked\" - a broad ban would have flagged every one of\nthose true statements as if it contradicted the badge. Running it\nagainst the existing corpus is what found the three drifted articles\nabove.\n\n搵到兩篇文早就做完但個徽章仲寫緊「移植緊」,而家攞返正:issue #31 (材質\n包三個出閘條件全部真係跑過)同 issue #44 (Pages 出版真係對住 GitHub 走\n完一次),兩篇都升做「已完成」,唔再靠得住個人講。仲執多三篇因為另一\n篇升級之後冇跟住改,舊句子仲話「未跑過」,其實隔籬篇早就跑咗。新加\n嘅測試就係為咗呢種漂移:一有已完成嘅文自己講返自己「未跑過」就爆錯,\n第日再有人升錯級唔使等人手執。",
