                details: "loadSchedule/saveSchedule and their four refs (schedule, loadingSchedule,\nscheduleFailure, savingSchedule) join owners/repositories/nameAvailability\nas the same kind of optional, bridge-probed state - canManageSchedule is\nfalse, and both methods are quiet no-ops, on a build without both bridge\nmethods, exactly like canListOwners and its siblings already degrade.\nsaveSchedule re-reads the status on a successful write rather than\ninventing one locally, because the workflow's own last-check fields are\nuntouched by turning scheduling on and a screen guessing them would show\na check that never happened. A refusal - most often \"this world has\nnever been uploaded\" - surfaces through scheduleFailure without a\npointless re-read.\n\nloadSchedule/saveSchedule 呢兩個function,同埋佢哋嗰四個ref\n(schedule、loadingSchedule、scheduleFailure、savingSchedule),而家同\nowners/repositories/nameAvailability埋一齊,做返嗰種靠bridge探路嘅\n選擇性state——build 冇齊兩個bridge method,canManageSchedule就係false,\n兩個method都靜靜地乜都唔做,同canListoxOwners嗰班兄弟退化法一樣。\nsaveSchedule 寫成功之後會重新讀一次狀態,唔會自己就地作一個出嚟——因\n為開排程呢個動作本身唔會掂到workflow自己嗰堆上次check嘅field,畫面\n自己作出嚟就會顯示一個從未發生過嘅check。寫嘢俾拒絕(最多見係「呢個\n世界從未上載過」)就會經scheduleFailure浮返出嚟,唔使再讀多次做無謂功。",
