                subject: "Wake up hourly, render only when the world actually changed",
                details: "scheduled-render.yml is the piece the render-actions CLI additions\nwere built for: it wakes on GitHub's schedule trigger every hour - the\nfinest cadence this feature offers, since a repository variable cannot\nchange a cron already baked into this file - asks schedule-due whether\nthe configured cadence says a check is actually due, and only then\ngathers one cheap snapshot (a checked-out world's fingerprint, a\nrelease asset's published digest/size/time, or a URL's cache headers)\nand hands it to schedule-check. A render is only dispatched on\n\"changed\"; \"unchanged\", \"unknown\" and \"error\" all record themselves in\nrepository variables and a run summary and stop there, having touched\nnothing but metadata.\n\nThis lane's own three world-sources reconcile cleanly with a fourth,\n\"git\", that landed in the same files while this was in flight - see\nthat commit for the story; nothing here fights it.\n\ndocs/scheduled-render.md covers configuration, the per-source honesty\nlimits, cost (an exact monthly check count, never a made-up runner-\nminute figure), failure modes and verification, and is linked from\nboth docs/README.md and render-in-actions.md.\n\n呢個叫醒鐘,每個鐘response一次,唔係「叫醒咗就一定郁手」。schedule-\nrender.yml 就係render-actions個CLI專登整落嚟嗰樣嘢:靠GitHub個schedule\ntrigger,每個鐘醒一次——因為repo variable改極都改唔到已經寫死喺呢份file\n嘅cron,所以呢個已經係呢個功能出得起嘅最密頻率——醒咗先問schedule-due\n而家個cadence係咪真係到鐘,到咗先去攞一份平嘅snapshot(已經checkout落\n嚟嘅世界指紋、release asset嘅digest/size/時間、又或者URL嘅cache\nheaders),再交畀schedule-check判。淨係「changed」先至會真係去dispatch\nrender;「unchanged」、「unknown」、「error」全部老老實實記落repo\nvariable同run summary就算數,乜嘢都冇碰過,得返metadata。\n\n呢條線自己嗰三種world-source,同期間喺同一批file度加落嚟嘅第四種\n「git」啱啱好夾埋一齊——嗰段古仔睇返嗰個commit,呢度冇同佢打交。\n\ndocs/scheduled-render.md 講晒配置、每種source嘅老實限制、成本(準確嘅\n每月check次數,絕對唔係作出嚟嘅runner分鐘數)、失敗情況同驗證,仲喺\ndocs/README.md同render-in-actions.md兩邊都駁咗link。",
