                subject: "Fix a real bug found by testing backups against live GitHub: not every 422 is a taken tag",
                details: "createBackupRelease treated every 422 from release creation as a tag\ncollision and said so unconditionally: \"already has a release tagged X ...\nstart the backup again to get a fresh tag.\" A live run against a brand-new,\nnever-pushed-to repository found this is wrong - GitHub answers the same\n422 status for \"this repository has no commits yet\", with a completely\ndifferent body (\"Repository is empty.\", no tag named at all). Retrying, as\nthe old message advised, would have failed identically forever, because\nthe real problem was never the tag.\n\nFixed by reading GitHub's structured errors[].code rather than trusting\nthe status alone: a genuine collision (code already_exists, or field\ntag_name) still gets the exact same \"start again for a fresh tag\" advice;\nan empty repository gets its own correct message naming the real cause and\nthe real fix (push at least one commit first); anything else still passing\nthrough GitHub's own words rather than a guess. Also adds the committed\nlive-GitHub test (backup.realGithub.test.ts, skipped by default per this\nproject's *.real*.test.ts convention) that found the bug in the first\nplace, packing, publishing, resuming and restoring a real backup against\nreal github.com.\n\n執到一個要真係撞落 GitHub 先睇得出嘅 bug: 個 422 唔係逢 422 都係話個 tag 已經\n有人用咗。新開一個未 push 過嘢嘅 repo 一 backup,GitHub 都係俾 422,但寫嘅係\n「呢個 repo 係空嘅」,同 tag 冇關係,舊碼照樣叫人「換個新 tag 再試」,試極都係\n死路一條。而家改為睇 GitHub 自己嗰個 errors[].code 嚟分真假,啱嘅畀啱嘅提示,\n唔啱嘅畀番真相。仲加埋個真係打去 github.com 嘅測試,依家預設唔行,但打嗰陣\n就係佢揾到呢條 bug。",
