                details: "The machines list already validated, persisted, and version-historied every\nsaved host with nothing secret in it (see remoteTargets.ts's own doc\ncomment); what it could not yet do was put your usual host near the top of\nthe list or hand you a second machine that mostly matches an existing one.\n\nremoteRecency.ts tracks, per machine id, the last time it was chosen for a\nrender - never sent anywhere, never part of the validated RemoteTarget shape,\nmirrored into the application-settings history the same way remoteTargets.ts\nmirrors the list itself. RunLocationCard.vue sorts the editor's list by it on\nevery load and every pick. RemoteTargetEditor.vue grows a Duplicate action\nbeside Edit and Forget: it opens the form pre-filled from an existing machine\nunder a fresh id and a \"Copy of {name}\" label, and saves nothing until the\nsame Check-and-save button that validates a brand new machine has validated\nthis one too.\n\nForgetting a saved machine stays behind no super-confirmation gate, on\npurpose: components/remote/RemoteTargetEditor.vue is already declared\n\"reversible\" in DESTRUCTIVE_FILES; a saved host carries no secret (the\nidentity file is a path this app never opens) and the same four short\nfields are typed again in under a minute, which is the standing that\npolicy test enforces rather than a gap in this pass.\n\n儲低嘅 SSH機終於識分邊部係你熟嘅：撳過用過嘅機而家會跳去清單頭，唔使成日喺一堆機入面搵返嗰部。仲加多咗個「複製」掣，\n撳一下就攞現有機嘅資料開返張表俾你改,新機有自己嘅id,乜都未儲,一定要撳返個Check掣過關先真係存到。忘記一部機依然唔使\n過兩條key嗰關 -- 呢部機本身冇密碼呢種嘢,四個欄半分鐘打返晒,呢個係嗰份destructive政策度講明嘅\"可以簡單返做\"個標準,\n唔係漏咗做。",
