                details: "A world does not have to be zipped up and carried here: if it already lives\non a machine the person owns and can reach over SSH, this reads it from\nthere. Linux gets rsync's real delta transfer through the connection and\ntransfer machinery remote/ already has; Windows - which almost never ships\nrsync - gets an honest scp fallback plus a PowerShell -EncodedCommand trick\nthat sidesteps the cmd-vs-PowerShell login-shell guessing game entirely, so\none remote command line works regardless of which shell sshd handed it to.\nA cheap size/mtime survey (find on POSIX, Get-ChildItem on Windows) answers\n\"did anything change\" without transferring a single region file, exposed as\npure functions for whatever drives scheduled rendering later. Host-key\ntrust, unreachable hosts, refused auth and a changed key all reuse the\nexisting remote/hostkey.ts and remote/failure.ts vocabulary rather than\ninventing a second one. 43 new tests against fake SSH/process runners; no\nreal host was harmed, or even contacted, in the making of this feature.\n\n一個世界唔使執好晒個袋先攞過嚟：如果佢本身就住喺你自己部機、SSH又摸得到，\n呢個功能直接去嗰度讀。Linux果邊靠rsync真係識埋差異傳輸，用返remote/\n已經有嘅連線同傳輸機器；Windows果邊——幾乎從來冇rsync——就老實咁降級去\nscp，仲加埋PowerShell嘅-EncodedCommand絕技，唔使估佢login shell係cmd\n定PowerShell，一條command line兩邊都掂。仲有個平靚正嘅檔案清單（POSIX用\nfind，Windows用Get-ChildItem），淨係睇size同mtime就知道有冇改過，一個\nregion檔都唔使搬，留返畀之後嘅排程render用。主機key信唔信、連唔到、\n密碼頂唔順、key換咗呢啲全部沿用返remote/嘅原班人馬，冇整多套詞出嚟。\n新增43條測試,用假嘅SSH/process runner——真.主機一隻都冇搞過。",
                category: "shell",
                areas: ["shell"],
