                subject: "Reach a world that lives in Docker: bind mount, named volume, or a container copy",
                details: "A world does not have to live on this machine's filesystem to be rendered - it can be\nsitting inside a running (or stopped) Minecraft server's container, mounted in as a bind\nmount or a named volume. This adds `main/dockerworld/`, the input-side counterpart to the\nin-flight SSH remote-render and git-repository lanes: given a container id and a mount, or\na bare volume name, it resolves the cheapest honest way to read it (straight off the host\nfilesystem when that is actually reachable, `docker cp` or a disposable helper container\notherwise), copies it incrementally, and refuses outright to read a running server's world\nwithout the caller explicitly accepting the torn-region-file risk that implies.\n\nEvery command runs through the same injectable CommandRunner runtime/docker.ts and\nremote/ssh.ts already use, so the identical logic answers for a local daemon or one reached\nover sshCommandRunner(...) with no second implementation; remote byte transport reuses the\nSSH lane's own FileTransfer (rsync-when-available, scp otherwise) rather than a parallel\ncopier. Nothing here ever deletes a destination file, so no destructive-action gate applies.\nIPC wiring (main-process only, local daemon) and tests land in the next commits.\n\n咪以為個世界一定要坐喺硬盤度先算數 - 佢住喺一個仲開緊嘅 Minecraft 伺服器個 container 入面都得,\n照樣影到相。而家加咗 main/dockerworld/,同已經開緊工嘅 SSH 遠端算圖、git repo 世界嗰兩條線一齊\n夾埋做「世界由邊度嚟」嗰塊拼圖:俾個 container id 加個掛載點,或者淨係一個 volume 名,佢會揀最平\n又老實嗰種讀法(host 檔案系統真係摷到就直接摷,唔得就用 docker cp 或者叫個用完即棄嘅 helper\ncontainer 幫手),用增量方式攞返嚟,而如果個伺服器仲開緊,絕對唔會靜雞雞讀住佢寫緊嗰啲檔案 -\n除非你自己講明肯博一鑊「讀到一半嘅殘缺 region 檔」嘅風險。",
