                subject: "Add the Cheap LFS restore engine backups never had",
                details: "The backups article claimed restoring hands a release to main/download/,\n\"the surface that already fetches parts, verifies each one, rejoins them and\nunpacks\". That was never true: main/download/ only understands a\n<name>.parts.json manifest beside <name>.001, <name>.002, ...; a backup's\nparts are named <archive>.NNN-sha16 with no .parts.json ever published, so\nmain/download/'s own discovery could not recognise a Cheap LFS release as a\nsplit download at all, let alone restore one. Nothing before this exercised\nthat path against a real release to find out, so the gap sat undetected\nbehind a comment that read as a decision.\n\nThis adds main/backup/restore.ts: a BackupRestoreRunner that reads a\nrelease's sidecar and pointer, refuses one whose upload never finished (no\npointer, no whole-file digest to trust), downloads every part with a\nresumable ranged request, translates the pointer into a\n@material-bluemap/parts PartsManifest in memory so the existing rejoin -\nper-part digest, resumable prefix verification, whole-file digest - is\nreused rather than reimplemented, then extracts the verified archive. Eight\ntests round-trip a real BackupRunner's upload through the new restorer byte\nfor byte, including the single-asset (unsplit) form, a stopped upload\nmissing its pointer, a corrupted part, a missing release, and cancellation.\n\n修返 backup 一直冇嘅嗰個「還原」按鈕 - 原來成日話交畀 downloads 嗰個 surface,\n但嗰個 surface 淨係識 .parts.json 嗰種包法,backup 自己嘅 part 命名方式佢連認都\n唔識,即係話呢粒掣由頭到尾都係得個講法冇個做法。而家真係寫咗個 restore.ts,\n將 pointer 翻譯做 parts 套件識嘅 manifest,咁樣 rejoin 嗰套驗證邏輯就唔使\n重新發明,八個測試證明成個流程由上傳到還原,啲位元係一模一樣。",
