                details: "Wire the desktop app's downloads bridge to main/worldsource/ instead of\nmain/download/ alone. discoverRelease, startDownload, cancelDownload and\nactiveDownloads now call worldsource:discover / worldsource:fetch /\nworldsource:cancel / worldsource:active, which understand any public\nGitHub repository and both split layouts (this project's own parts\nmanifest and a plain sha256sum SHA256SUMS listing) - not just this\nproject's own manifest-shaped releases. A pasted link resolving to an\nowner and a repository was a doc's promise about code that did not exist\nyet; the code existed all along in main/worldsource/, fully tested and\nsimply never called.\n\ntoBridgeDiscoveryResult and toBridgeCoordinates in the new\nworldSourceBridge.ts are the seam that lets this happen without changing\nwhat the bridge has always promised the interface: a checksum-list\nworld's `kind` becomes the same `split` flag a manifest world's always\nwas. Both are pure and Electron-free on purpose, so they get a real\nvitest suite instead of \"trust the plumbing\".\n\n以前份 downloader 淨係識揸自己嗰份 parts.json,人哋release嘅 SHA256SUMS 就當佢冇到,\n仲要淨限呢個project自己repo。而家全部撥去 worldsource,邊個repo都睇得,兩種split\n都識,連個link都幫你解返做owner/repo。個橋接層執到七七八八,而家先叫真係接埋線。",
