                details: "The article's own callout used to say plainly that nothing had ever run a real\nChunker jar against a real Bedrock world through this app - the CLI contract\nwas read from Chunker's source, never observed. That gap is closed: a new\nopt-in test (BEDROCK_E2E=1) unpacks a genuine Bedrock world (one of Hive\nGames' own MIT integration-test fixtures, committed at\nbedrock/__fixtures__/BEDROCK_R12.zip), fetches the real chunker-cli-1.19.1.jar\nfrom github.com, checks it against the pinned SHA-256 (it matched - the pin\nis correct, not just self-consistent), finds a real JVM, and drives\nregisterBedrockHandlers' actual detect/fetchChunker/convert handlers with\nnothing injected but IpcMain. It converted for real: \"Converting from Bedrock\n1.12.0 to Java 1.21.4\", \"Conversion complete!\", exit 0, real region files,\nand a real bedrock-conversion.json written and read back. Status moves from\n\"ported-unverified\" to \"shipped\", with an honest new callout naming what one\nsmall fixture does not cover: batching and out-of-memory recovery against a\nreal large world, and real mid-JVM cancellation. Also corrected the article's\nstale test count (121 tests / seven files -> the real 134 / ten, plus this\neleventh opt-in file).\n\n過去嗰個 callout 老實講到出晒面：呢個功能由頭到尾都未同真嘅 Chunker、真嘅 JVM、\n真嘅 Bedrock 世界打過交道，成套 CLI 合約都係讀 Chunker 原始碼估出嚟，未曾眼見\n為實。而家補返呢個窿：整咗個 BEDROCK_E2E=1 先至跑嘅測試，解壓一個真.\nBedrock 世界（Hive Games 自己 MIT 授權嘅集成測試 fixture,放喺\nbedrock/__fixtures__/BEDROCK_R12.zip),由 github.com 落返個真身\nchunker-cli-1.19.1.jar,同源碼入面釘死嘅 SHA-256 對過(啱晒 - 證明個釘唔係\n得個天九咁啱得個天九,係真係啱),搵一個機上面真.JVM,再用真.\nIpcMain 去揸實際嘅 detect/fetchChunker/convert 三個 handler,乜嘢都無 mock。\n真係轉咗:「Converting from Bedrock 1.12.0 to Java 1.21.4」、\n「Conversion complete!」,exit code 0,真.region 檔案,仲有真.\nbedrock-conversion.json 寫低再讀返出嚟啱晒。狀態由「移植咗但未驗證」\n轉做「已上線」,新增一個老實嘅 callout 講清楚呢個細細嘅 fixture 未覆蓋到\n乜嘢:大世界嘅分批轉換、真.OOM 恢復、同真.JVM 中途取消轉換。\n順便執返篇文舊咗嘅測試數(121/七個檔案 -> 真身係134/十個,加埋呢個\n第十一個 opt-in 檔案)。",
