                subject: "Rebuild the landing page as a rebrand, not a retouch",
                details: "The hero gets a kicker line, a gradient-mesh background pulled from the\nprimary/secondary container tones, an isometric-block motif bled off one\ncorner via clip-path, a display-scale title with its own weight and\ntracking override, and a secondary \"See what changed\" action beside the\ndownload button. The screenshot gallery -- the most visually convincing\nthing on the page -- moves from four viewport-heights down to directly\nafter the hero. The stats section becomes a desktop bento grid (one stat\nspanning two cells, oversized tabular numerals) that collapses to a\nhorizontal scroll-snapped strip on phones. Feature cards and engine cards\npick up real elevation and a hover lift; screenshot frames drop to the\nsmallest corner radius on the shape scale so they read as photographs\nagainst the hero's exaggerated roundness. A `home.heroKicker` /\n`home.changelogButtonLabel` pair joins the language catalogue in English\nand Cantonese, and the hero's own pill-shaped controls get a bilingual\nline-wrap fix so the Cantonese half no longer runs into the English half\nwith no space.\n\nThis commit is scoped to exactly this lane's work via `git apply --cached`\nagainst the current index rather than `git commit -- <pathspec>`, because\nmain.ts, content.css and strings.ts are shared with the documentation-index\nand changelog lanes editing the same files concurrently; their in-progress\nhunks are left exactly as uncommitted in the working tree, ready for them\nto commit under their own name. One shared selector, `.mb-page-kicker`\nriding alongside `.mb-hero-kicker`, is included because it was written\ndirectly onto this pass's own rule rather than sitting in an independent\nregion of the file.\n\n冇心機再執少少就話係「全新設計」,呢鑊真係推倒重嚟:標題大到爆錶,\n截圖由第四屏拉到頭版,統計數字變晒 bento 格仔,手機仲有得拖動。\n順手執返雙語版嗰個「撞埋一齊冇位隔」嘅老毛病。呢個 commit 淨係影住\n自己嗰份,隔籬條 lane 手頭嘅嘢冇被順手篤咗入嚟。",
