                subject: "Voice the site's chrome that content rendering adds: badges, page titles, error boundary",
                details: "The catalogue reached settings, search, tabs, notifications, the palette\nand the confirm gate, but everything shell/renderBlocks.ts and main.ts\ngenerate around an article -- the callout tone badge, the code-sample\naria-label, the Shipped/Ported/Specified status badge, the Application/\nEngine/Delivery/Contracts category heading, the phase table's caption\nand columns, \"Suggested articles\", \"Sources\" -- stayed hardcoded English\nregardless of language mode. The Documentation and Screenshots page\ntitles duplicated an already-voiced tab label in a second, unvoiced\nstring that could drift from it; both now read the one source of truth.\nThe hero's release-status eyebrow and the fatal-boot-failure notice\n(best-effort: a fresh I18n/Preferences pair, discarded for the plain\nEnglish fallback if constructing it is itself what failed) are voiced\ntoo. The Screenshots page had no command-palette entry at all; it now\nhas one, matching every sibling page.\n\nArticle prose itself -- paragraph/list/table/definition/callout body\ntext an author wrote -- stays literal English on purpose: it is\ndocumentation content, not chrome, the same line packages/ui draws\nbetween a surface's copy and its data. Comments at each boundary say\nso explicitly rather than leaving the split to be inferred.\n\nAdded a FACTS tier to the site's i18n catalogue (packages/site had none\nbefore this, unlike packages/ui's mandatory version) scoped to the\nentries this pass introduces that state a real claim -- a release is\nverified, a page failed to start -- plus an em-dash ban across the\nwhole catalogue, which cost nothing since none existed. Both are\nguarded in strings.test.ts.\n\n三個獨立嘅 badge 詞典同一堆散落嘅英文字，而家全部經返 i18n 度攞字，唔使個\n訪客揀咗廣東話都要睇英文 badge。個 Documentation 標題以前同個分頁標籤各自\n各精彩，而家改返用返同一個 key，唔會有日兩個字唔同咗都冇人發現。開機失敗\n嗰個畫面都試住講返訪客揀嘅語言先，救唔到先退返做英文。仲加咗個 FACTS 機\n制，專釘住呢批新字入面嘅事實唔會俾搞笑等級沖走。",
