                subject: "Register GlossaryTerm.vue's popover in the menu-coverage guard",
                details: "A new <v-menu> (the term-definition popover) shipped without joining\nmenuCoverage.test.ts's REGISTRY, tripping the \"registers every file the\nsweep finds\" guard. It is one paragraph and a \"Read more\" link, so it is\nmarked not-applicable with a reason rather than grown a search field it\nhas nothing to filter.\n\nGuards don't do irony, but if they did: the guard that catches\nundocumented menus was, itself, undocumented for one menu. Filed the\npaperwork. 個新彈出視窗out街唔知會之下，冚咗個 guard 一鑊。呢個 popover\n淨係得一段字同一條連結，乜都冇得搜，所以老實claim做「not-applicable」，\n唔會為咗過test夾硬塞個搜尋格落去。",
