                subject: "Stop the tour's own doc comment tripping the catalogue scanner it explains",
                details: "catalogueCoverage.test.ts's regex reads source text for a literal, quoted\nt() call, which is exactly what \"phaseLabel/adviseOnFailure already draw\nthis line the same way: a plain switch with a literal t(\"key\", \"fallback\")\nper case\" contained inside a doc comment. Harmless - the surface still hit\n100% coverage either way, since the fake key never entered the required\nCOVERED_SURFACES assertion, only the informational leftover-count report -\nbut a comment explaining \"the scanner reads source text\" that the scanner\nitself then reads as a source call is the kind of thing worth not leaving\nin place. Reworded to describe the shape without spelling out a quoted key.\n\n叫呢個掃描器唔好被解釋緊佢自己嘅註解呃親\n\ncatalogueCoverage.test.ts 個 regex 淨係睇原始碼入面一個真正加咗引號嘅 t()\n呼叫,但我之前一句解釋嘅註解入面啱啱好就寫咗一個睇落好似咁樣嘅例子。冇實際\n影響——呢個 surface 兩種情況都係 100% 覆蓋,個假 key 從來冇入到必要嘅\nCOVERED_SURFACES 斷言度,淨係入咗個資訊性嘅「仲差幾多」報告——不過一句解釋\n「呢個掃描器淨係睇原始碼」嘅註解,竟然俾同一個掃描器當真嘢讀咗,始終唔係\n一件應該留低嘅事。而家改咗寫法,講返個形狀,唔再拼埋一個加咗引號嘅假 key。",
