                subject: "Restyle the settings tab row as an M3 segmented button group",
                details: "The settings General/Language/Appearance/Accessibility/Data row used to be\nthe exact same underlined text-tab styling as the primary chrome strip one\nlevel up, so a settings surface and the top-level tab bar were visually the\nsame control worn twice. It is now a pill-shaped segmented group with the\nselected segment on primary-container, matching Material's own segmented\nbutton rather than reusing the underline. Same buttons, same role=\"tab\"\nelements, same keyboard model, same per-tab search and badge counts, same\nappearance-editor hooks — TabStrip.ts and the primary chrome it belongs to\nare untouched, and remain the one browser-style strip in the product.\n\n嘅settings個tab bar本來同最頂嗰條chrome tab bar撞衫,兩個都係底線嗰種,\n睇落好似同一條友揸兩份工。而家改成藥丸形嘅segmented group,揀中嗰格變\nprimary-container底色,keyboard、搜尋、徽章數字、appearance編輯全部冇少\n一樣嘢,淨係個樣唔再同頂欄撞款。",
