                subject: "Fix the viewer-menu search never filtering its own option lists; clear the settings-drawer search of any bug",
                details: "The visual audit's Priority 3 finding (design/docs/visual-audit-2026-08-05.md)\nflagged two search surfaces, settings-search.png and menu-search.png, as\npossibly showing a match count while leaving the rendered list unfiltered.\nSettled both by mounting the real components and reading the query results\nback from the DOM rather than guessing from a screenshot - the two needed\nopposite verdicts.\n\nThe Settings drawer (AppSettings.vue) is not a bug. Only the active tab's\nsection is ever mounted, so a search there was never going to hide content:\nit lists matching sections as destinations to jump to, exactly the way the\noptions editor lists its own cross-screen matches, and clicking one switches\ntabs. AppSettings.test.ts already has a test titled precisely \"lists only\nthe sections that match, as destinations rather than as hidden content\" that\nlocks this in - the audit's own screenshot showed a real, working design,\nnot a missing filter. captions.md's \"filtering the drawer down to the\nsettings that match\" is loose but not false; that stays a caption-wording\nnote, not a functional defect.\n\nThe viewer-menu search (SettingsMenu.vue) had a real defect. Switch- and\nslider-based groups (Lighting, Render Distance, Map Controls, Free-Flight\nControls) filtered their own members correctly - searching \"sunlight\"\nalways hid the Ambient-Light slider beside it. But the four groups built on\nMenuOptionList (View/Controls, Resolution, Theme, Language) handed it their\nentire, unfiltered options array regardless of the query, because\nMenuOptionList itself filters nothing - once a group's own v-if passed\nbecause any single member matched, every sibling option rendered whether or\nnot it individually matched. Searching \"Perspective\" kept showing \"Flat\"\nand \"Free-Flight\" beside it, the exact \"9 of 60 but the panel looks\nunfiltered\" shape the audit described.\n\nFixed by filtering what each MenuOptionList actually receives down to the\noptions show() itself would keep - the group's own title plus that one\noption's name, the same two-candidate rule every switch/slider group\nalready applies per member - so the deliberate \"searching a category's own\nname reveals the whole category\" behaviour survives untouched while a\nspecific option name now genuinely narrows the list.\n\nNew SettingsMenu.test.ts mounts the component with a three-view-mode app and\nproves both halves: the four MenuOptionList groups now hide a non-matching\nsibling on a specific query while still showing the whole category on a\ncategory-name query, and the switch/slider groups' existing correct\nfiltering is pinned alongside it as a control. 5 new tests, 76 settings/menu\ntests green overall, a clean packages/ui typecheck and eslint pass.\n\n視覺審查話settings-search.png同menu-search.png呢兩張相,睇落個計數字啱,但\n畫面成隻豬咁樣冇篩過。今次唔靠估相,直接開返個真.組件,打個字入去,喺\nDOM度讀返個結果 —— 兩個原來要判唔同嘅生死。\n\n設定櫃桶(AppSettings.vue)嗰個查極都冇嘢,根本唔算蟲。佢淨係開緊嗰版先\n會裝落嚟,所以搜索由頭到尾都冇嘢好收埋——佢係列出邊版啱,俾你揀跳去邊,\n同個設定編輯器自己嗰個跨頁搜尋一模一樣做法。AppSettings.test.ts 老早有條\n測試就係專登叫呢個名嘅:「淨係列出啱嘅版,當係個目的地,唔係收埋咗嘅內\n容」——即係一早已經釘死呢個做法。個相顯示緊嘅其實係做對咗嘅設計,唔係\n漏咗嘅篩選。captions.md 嗰句「將櫃桶篩到淨返啱嘅設定」講得鬆咗啲,但唔\n算講大話,呢個留低做返個文案筆記,唔算功能上嘅蟲。\n\n反而個地圖選單搜索(SettingsMenu.vue)先係真係有蟲。撳掣、拉杆嗰啲組\n(燈光、渲染距離、地圖控制、自由飛行控制)本身係篩得啱嘅——搵「陽光」\n真係會收埋隔籬個「環境光」拉杆。但係四個用 MenuOptionList 起嘅組(視角\n控制、解像度、主題、語言)乜都冇篩過,成個未過濾嘅選項清單照樣派出去,\n因為 MenuOptionList 自己根本唔識篩選——只要嗰組嘅 v-if 因為隨便一粒選項\n啱咗就開咗,入面邊個都照全部畫晒。搵「透視」都仲見到「平面」同「自由\n飛行」喺隔籬,一模一樣「9之60,但成版睇落冇篩過」嘅衰相。\n\n而家修好咗:每個 MenuOptionList 真正收到嘅嘢,篩到淨返 show() 自己會揀\n嘅選項——嗰組自己個標題,加埋嗰粒選項自己個名,同撳掣拉杆組每粒成員一\n早用緊嗰兩個條件一樣。搵成個分類個名,仍然會見晒成個分類,但搵得夠精\n準,而家就真係篩得返窄。",
                category: "interface",
