                subject: "Publish RELEASES and the Squirrel .nupkg as their own release assets, not only zipped",
                details: "The updater this app ships (design/packages/app/src/main/update/feed.ts) resolves a\npackaged Windows build's feed to update.electronjs.org, which speaks Squirrel.Windows by\nfetching RELEASES and the matching .nupkg straight from a GitHub release with a plain\nHTTPS GET - github.com/<repo>/releases/download/<tag>/<filename>. Every release so far has\nonly ever shipped that pair zipped inside the \"extras\" archive, alongside a test world\nnobody's updater needs. A direct request for either file 404s: curled against the current\nlatest release, both RELEASES and the full .nupkg came back \"404 Not Found\" while the\ninstaller itself answered \"200 OK\" right next to them. The feed resolver, the failure\nclassifier and 280-odd tests all assume a working Squirrel feed and none of them catch\nthis, because the gap is not in the app - it is in what the release workflow chooses to\nupload, and nothing before this exercised a real HTTPS GET against a real published asset.\nNet effect: every installed copy's automatic-update check can see a newer release exists\nand can never fetch it, silently, forever, since the failure classifier has no code for\n\"the server told me exactly where to look and there was nothing there.\" Adds the same\n`installer-out/*.nupkg` and `installer-out/RELEASES` globs already used to populate the\nextras archive to the loose release-asset list, so both exist as real top-level assets too\n- the extras copy stays, for whoever wants the whole update set in one file.\n\n呢個程式嘅自動更新一直靠得住个update.electronjs.org去攞RELEASES同個.nupkg,佢哋兩個嘅\n下載位一直得個樣,冇真身:淨係包咗喺extras嗰個zip入面,直接攞就係404。即係話部機一直查\n得出有新版,但係永遠攞唔到,靜雞雞咁壞足全程,連個錯誤分類器都冇一條係諗住呢種「話咗你\n喺邊但個位冇嘢」嘅衰法。而家將呢兩隻嘢一齊寫做正式嘅release資產,唔止收埋喺個zip度。",
