                subject: "Site: publish a newcomer glossary, reachable from the install article",
                details: "The site assumed a reader already knew what \"tile\", \"engine\", \"project\", \"the\nflattening\" and a dozen other project-specific words meant, and used them from the\nfirst article onward with nothing to point at. Added glossary.ts: fifteen terms in\nplain language, grouped by concept rather than alphabetised, with a dedicated\n\"failure modes\" section for the traps a newcomer actually hits (a Minecraft map item\nis not this project's map; \"the engine\" without a name means whichever one currently\nrenders). It carries the same five required sections, sources design/HANDOFF.md's own\nagent-facing glossary as the term list it stays consistent with, and is linked first\nfrom the install article's suggested reading so it is the natural next stop.\n\nNo in-app equivalent exists yet; a concurrent onboarding workflow may add one to the\ndesktop application and possibly its own docs/ article. This article says so plainly\nin its status note rather than implying the two already agree, and is written to\nreconcile with that work once it lands rather than to pre-empt it.\n\n網站以前由第一篇文章開始就一路用晒 tile、engine、project、the flattening 呢啲字,\n估晒讀者已經識,連解釋都冇。而家加咗個 glossary.ts,十五個術語用返日常話解釋,重\n特登有個「常見誤解」部分,講返新人最易撞板嗰啲位(Minecraft 遊戲入面嗰個地圖係\n另一回事)。由 install 文章第一個建議連結指返過去,等啱啱裝完就見到。",
