                subject: "Bring settings, content and search surfaces onto the M3 token layer",
                details: "Three site stylesheets carried genuine Material Design 3 tokens for most of\ntheir rules and then quietly switched to hand-picked pixels the moment a\nnewer feature (discovery, changelog, command palette, date-range picker,\nsettings rows, the appearance editor, the colour picker) got appended in a\nhurry. settings.css alone had 17 off-scale 6px/10px/14px spacings and eleven\nfont sizes that sat nowhere on the declared 15-step type scale (0.82rem,\n0.95rem, 1.05rem, 1.3rem...); content.css's discovery/changelog/palette\nblock, named specifically because it says \"share the same M3 card anatomy\"\nin its own comment, did not; search.css re-derived every colour, radius and\nmotion value as a second --mbm-* layer with its own hard-coded hex\nfallbacks and a dead prefers-color-scheme block that data-theme's\nhigher specificity had already made unreachable.\n\nEvery one of those values now resolves through --md-sys-spacing-*,\n--md-sys-typescale-*-size/-weight/-font and --md-sys-motion-duration-*/\n-easing-* instead of a literal the next edit could silently drift from.\nsearch.css's colour/shape/motion aliases point straight at the system\ntokens with no duplicate palette and no fallback hex to fall out of step\nwith tokens.css. Nothing else moved: same class names, same DOM, same\ncomponents -- 232 site tests and the production build (with its base-path\ngate) pass unchanged.\n\n執嘢囉!settings.css 嗰陣時自己諗到 6px 呢個「靈感數字」,同埋 1.05rem 呢個\n無出處嘅字號,結果全個 spacing scale 得返佢一個唔跟規矩。而家全部要返去讀\ntokens.css 嗰份「操行手冊」,唔准再自由發揮。search.css 更加正一戲肉:自己\n起多一套顏色系統,仲要留埋十六進制後備值,好似驚 tokens.css 唔見咗噉。而家\n拆晒個假天花板,直接用返正牌 token,少個副本少個煩惱。",
