                subject: "Site: document the world-sources release-downloads path, tidy two blank table headers",
                details: "release-downloads.ts described only this project's own worlds.json parts manifest, while\npackages/app/src/main/worldsource (docs/world-sources.md) had already shipped a second,\nindependent capability: pasting a link to any public GitHub repository or tagged release,\nand understanding the far more common plain-sha256sum split layout beside this project's\nown manifest. The article now says so, cites the module and the doc, and a new\ncontent.test.ts regression pins both facts so the gap cannot quietly reopen.\n\nAlso fixed: two comparison tables (bedrock-worlds.ts, and one landing in an earlier commit\nhere alongside this work) used an empty string \"\" as the row-label column's header, which\nthe site's own \"no blank strings\" copy-rule test correctly refuses to let through. Swapped\nin the single space the rule explicitly carves out for exactly this case.\n\n呢篇 release-downloads 文章一直净係識得講自己嘅 parts manifest,人哋 worldsource module\n早就識得攞第二個 GitHub repo嘅 release,重識得睇最常見嗰種 SHA256SUMS 散裝法,篇文一直\n唔知有咁嘢,而家補返呢個事實仲加咗測試睇實佢。順手執返兩個比較表格個空白表頭 - 用返\n測試話俾你聽准用嘅嗰個空格,唔係得個吉。",
