                date: "2026-08-05T13:14:20-04:00",
                subject: "Fix the repair panel's agent chip clipping its own sentence at the docked-right width",
                details: "The Diagnostics status chip carries a full explanatory sentence from `repair/agent.ts`\n(\"There is no 'opencode' command on this account's PATH...\") rather than a short label,\nbut Vuetify's chip content is single-line and non-wrapping by default and the flex row\naround it never told the chip it was allowed to shrink. At the settings panel's default\ndocked-right width the sentence is wider than the chip, so the tail of it was drawn past\nthe panel's edge with no ellipsis, no scroll and no way to ever read it - confirmed live\nby installing the real v0.1.0-build.378 Squirrel installer on a headless desktop and\nopening Settings -> Diagnostics at the default dock width. `.mb-repair__agent .v-chip`\ngets `min-width: 0` so it can shrink inside the flex row instead of overflowing it, and\n`.v-chip__content` gets `white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere` so the sentence\nwraps onto more than one line once it does, matching the same min-width-plus-wrap shape\n`UpdateStatusRow.vue` already uses for its own long status text. CSS-only: RepairPanel's\n6 existing tests still pass and the production bundle carries the new rules unchanged.\n\n隻「自動修理」樣板入面嗰粒藥丸仔一直吞緊自己嗰句說話:句嘢老早過咗版面就畀硬生生𠝹斷,\n冇省略號冇scroll,想睇埋成句都冇門。而家教識個flex仔畀塊藥丸縮返皮,再教塊藥丸自己識得\n換行,句嘢終於見得返日光。純CSS改動,原有六個測試照跑照過。",
