                subject: "Add site articles for world discovery and Bedrock conversion; correct a stale \"pending\" CI claim",
                details: "The 35-article site registry had two shipped, in-app-docs-bundled features with no\narticle and no mention anywhere in the run: the wizard's first step (finding worlds\nalready on the machine, plus any mounted folders) and Bedrock world detection and\nChunker conversion. Both now have dedicated articles (world-discovery, bedrock-worlds),\nreachable from the landing page through world-reading's suggested list, with their own\nbehaviour/configuration/failure-modes/security/verification sections and doc links added\nadditively to links.ts.\n\nSeparately, ROADMAP.md and HANDOFF.md both asserted that CI run 30960216270 and Pages run\n30960216143 \"remain pending\" for commit 54559eb. They do not: gh run view shows both\ncompleted over a day ago, Pages succeeded and CI was cancelled rather than passed. A\nreader was being told an outcome was still unknown when it was in fact known and\nunfavourable, so both files now state plainly that the runs finished and that CI never\nactually verified that commit.\n\n跟住幫個文檔網補返兩篇成日都冇人記得嘅文章：wizard 第一步識自己揾世界，同埋\nBedrock 世界識別同用 Chunker 轉檔,呢兩樣嘢喺 app 入面實實在在出咗街,個網站\n35 篇文入面居然一篇都冇提過,好似冇發生過咁。而家補返 world-discovery 同\nbedrock-worlds 兩篇,由 world-reading 嗰篇撳得到,五段嘢齊晒。\n\n順手執多樣嘢:ROADMAP.md 同 HANDOFF.md 都寫住嗰兩個 run \"重等緊\",但用 gh\nrun view 一查,原來一日幾前就跑完:Pages 過咗,CI 就俾人取消咗,唔係\"未有結果\"\n係\"有結果但唔靚仔\"。而家兩份文都改返做老實講。",
