                subject: "Fix the Cantonese funny-level caption landing on top of its own tick label",
                details: "The same visual audit found 中間落墨 (\"Balanced\" in Cantonese), the current-\nlevel line under the Cantonese funny-level slider, rendering stacked on top\nof the slider's own \"1\" tick label - in both places this component mounts,\nthe first-run wizard and the Settings drawer's Language and tone section -\nwhile the English \"Balanced\" sat cleanly below its own \"1\". Vuetify's slider\nticks sit a fixed offset below the track rather than contributing to the\nslider's own document-flow height, so the caption's clearance depended\nentirely on its own line box; a CJK font's line-height metrics running\ntaller than the Latin fallback's at the same font-size was enough to close\nthat gap for one language and leave it open for the other. Gives the\ncaption an explicit top margin and line-height instead of the browser's\nfont-dependent defaults, so the gap holds regardless of which font a given\nlanguage happens to fall back to. A CSS-source regression test pins both\nvalues and confirms the fix reaches both mounted surfaces through this one\nshared component.\n\n搞掂咗廣東話搞笑程度個「而家幾搞笑」個描述,一路都疊埋喺個拉桿自己嗰個\n「1」刻度數字度,英文版嗰句「Balanced」就企定定喺下面,乜事都冇。兩個\n地方裝呢個組件都中晒招:首次執行嘅精靈、同埋設定櫃桶入面「語言與語氣」\n嗰欄。原來 Vuetify 個拉桿嘅刻度數字位,唔算落個拉桿自己嘅版面高度度,\n所以個描述同佢隔幾遠,全靠自己嗰行字嘅行高度事;廣東話用嘅字型行高\n啱啱好高過英文果隻,兩種語言就咁分咗差。而家俾個描述一個實牙實齒嘅頂\n邊距同行高,唔再靠瀏覽器揀邊個字型嚟話事,咁樣個空隙先至穩陣。加咗個\n睇原始碼嘅回歸測試,釘實呢兩個數值,順便確認呢個共用組件真係兩邊都影\n到。",
                category: "interface",
                areas: ["interface"],
                files: 2,
