                subject: "Fix: the docs browser's index and search results ellipsed titles with no recovery",
                details: "`<v-list-item :title=\"article.title\">` binds Vuetify's own `title`\n*prop* -- the text it renders -- never an HTML `title` attribute\n(`VListItem.js` only ever calls `toDisplayString(props.title)`), and\n`.v-list-item-title` defaults to `overflow: hidden; text-overflow:\nellipsis; white-space: nowrap`. The real longest article title this\nrepository ships, `docs/appearance-editors.md`'s own 85-character\nheading, truncates under that default with no hover tooltip for a\nsighted reader to recover it from (only the aria-label reached a screen\nreader). Fixed in both places this pattern appeared -- the category\nindex and the flat search-result list -- by moving the title into\nVuetify's own `#title` slot with a plain `<span :title=\"...\">`, which is\na genuine DOM attribute rather than a component prop, while keeping the\nsame `.v-list-item-title` wrapper and its ellipsis. A new test finds the\nreal longest bundled article title and asserts it survives as a native,\nhoverable attribute.\n\nDocumentation 個標題俾「…」食咗都追唔返：喺 `<v-list-item>`度綁\n`:title=\"article.title\"` 淨係綁到 Vuetify 自己嗰個顯示用嘅 title prop，\n從來都唔係一個真正嘅 HTML title attribute，所以 `.v-list-item-title`\n預設嘅 ellipsis 一剪，滑鼠用戶就冇得停低隻手指睇返全名（得返\nscreen reader 先睇到嗰個 aria-label）。而家兩處都改用 `#title` slot，入面\n擺返個真係識用 title attribute 嘅 `<span>`，用返本身資料庫入面最長嗰篇\n文章標題（85 個字）做測試，證明佢唔會再俾剪走。",
