                sha: "76018284492955b7a80d666bd6ec0c35cb9e3154",
                shortSha: "7601828449",
                date: "2026-08-05T12:39:07-04:00",
                subject: "Fix: a long marker set id could overflow its own panel header",
                details: "`.mb-config-markers__title` (the marker set's own id, shown as its\nexpansion-panel header) had only `font-weight` set, inside Vuetify's own\n`.v-expansion-panel-title` -- a flex row with no `min-width: 0` of its\nown. A flex child's min-width defaults to its unwrapped content size, and\na marker set id is arbitrary user text with no length limit and usually\nno spaces to break at (it is a slug), so a long one overflowed the header\nhorizontally instead of wrapping, pushing the \"N markers\" count sideways\nor past the panel's own edge -- the exact class of bug the appearance\neditor's own zero-height tab strip came from this session. Fixed with\n`min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere` on the title span and\n`flex-shrink: 0` on the count so it stays put. A `?raw` CSS-source test\npins both properties, and a mount test proves a long, space-free id\nrenders in full rather than silently losing part of itself.\n\nMarker set 個名冧咗都唔知：`.v-expansion-panel-title` 本身係冇 min-width 嘅\nflex row，我哋自己嗰個 title span 淨係識 font-weight，乜都冇補，於是一個又長\n又冇位斷開嘅 id（好似 slug 咁）就直情谷穿個 panel header，將「N markers」嗰粒\n數都撞歪咗 -- 同呢個 session 出現過嘅 appearance editor 縮到冇高度嗰單嘢係\n同一個病根。而家補返 min-width:0 同 overflow-wrap:anywhere，仲有\nflex-shrink:0 揸住粒數唔郁得。",
                category: "interface",
                areas: ["interface"],
                files: 2,
