                date: "2026-08-05T07:53:36-04:00",
                subject: "Fix MarkerMenu.test.ts's flaky filters-open assertion: give it its own localStorage",
                details: "Run 31001430770 (tip 2a06e19) failed the same clean way the last two did: Test\nFiles 1 failed | 476 passed (477), the wrapper correctly declined to retry it\nbecause a real failure was reported alongside the unrelated RPC-heartbeat error.\nThis time: \"mirrors under the markerFiltersOpen key when the filters panel is\ncollapsed\" expected recordAppSetting(\"markerFiltersOpen\", false) and got\n(\"markerFiltersOpen\", true) instead - the toggle read backwards.\n\nIt would not reproduce. Not running the file alone (7/7, five times in a row),\nnot running the whole local suite (477/477), not running it alongside every\nother file that touches this exact mechanism, three times over. That itself is\nthe diagnosis: this document's jsdom origin is opaque, so real `localStorage`\nthrows on every access - the same reason AppSettings.test.ts, ProfileManager\n.test.ts, CommandPalette.test.ts and tabs/TabbedNavigation.test.ts each install\ntheir own map-backed stand-in instead of relying on it. MarkerMenu.test.ts\ninstalled none. `MarkerMenu.vue`'s own readFiltersOpen()/its filters-open\nwatcher wrap every access in try/catch expecting exactly this, so without a\nstand-in of its own this file's `filtersOpen` always happens to start `true`\nand the mirroring test always happens to pass - right up until it runs in a\nworker that already holds a *working* `globalThis.localStorage` some other\nfile installed via `Object.defineProperty`, at which point this file silently\ninherits that stand-in and whatever `material-bluemap-marker-filters-open` key\nsome earlier, unrelated test left behind. Vitest does not guarantee that\nmutation is undone between files sharing a worker, and which files share a\nworker is not something a test author controls or a `git log` entry can see -\nwhich is exactly why two different CI runs hit it and five-plus identical\nlocal attempts, including three deliberately run alongside every file capable\nof causing it, did not.\n\nInstalled this file's own stand-in `localStorage` in `beforeAll`, the same map-\nbacked shape every sibling file above already uses, and clear it in\n`beforeEach` so no test - in this describe block or \"the sort control\" above\nit - can leave a value for the next one to inherit. This does not touch what\nany test asserts; it only stops the assertion depending on which other 476\nfiles happened to share this one's worker.\n\nVerified locally: `vitest run` on this file alone (7/7, unchanged), and three\nrepeated combined runs against every localStorage-installing sibling\n(AppSettings.test.ts, ProfileManager.test.ts, CommandPalette.test.ts,\ntabs/TabbedNavigation.test.ts) - 5 files, 128 tests, all green each time.\n`vue-tsc --noEmit` and `eslint` both clean.\n\n執嗰個掣, 開嗰吓關嗰吓, 喺自己間房度試極都冇事,叫埋成班鄰居一齊試都冇事,\n去到 CI 先發爛渣。原來唔怪得個掣, 怪隔籬房: 呢間房自己冇裝『唔記得』嘅\n牌, 隔籬房裝咗個真㗎, 有陣時兩間房碰巧用番同一份地方,佢哋唔執手尾,\n呢間房執手尾嗰陣執到人哋啲嘢。而家自己間房裝返塊自己嘅牌, 唔使睇隔籬做咩。",
                category: "interface",
                areas: ["interface"],
                files: 1,
