                date: "2026-08-05T07:35:45-04:00",
                subject: "Close issue #32: SQL storage proven cross-compatible with upstream's Java engine",
                details: "Issue #32's last open acceptance item — a map upstream's Java CLI writes into\nSQL storage, read correctly by this port, and the reverse — is now proven,\nboth directions, over a real mariadb:11.4.7 Docker container. Direction 1:\nupstream's real CLI rendered the standard 1000x1000 oracle fixture straight\ninto SQL storage; this port's SQLStorage read every tile and render-state\ngrid back byte-identical to a Java-rendered file-storage control (961/961\nhires, 24/24 lowres, both metadata documents, every deterministic\nrender-state field). Direction 2: this port's engine wrote the same fixture\ninto a second database; upstream's own CLI, run genuinely webserver-only\nwith no map ever loaded, served every tile and document back byte-identical\nover real HTTP through its production MapStorageRequestHandler route.\n\nNew committed, re-runnable script: tools/oracle/sql-crosscompat.mjs. It\nreuses the oracle harness's existing machinery rather than reinventing it -\nlib/javaOracle.mjs for the jar/world, and lib/renderstate.mjs's\ndiffRenderState (already trusted by compare.mjs's own Phase D gate and\ncovered by selftest.mjs) to separate real divergences from the wall-clock\nrender/update timestamps two independent renders cannot share. render-ts.mjs\ngrew a --storage-driver sql mode so the same TS-engine render driver\ncompare.mjs already used can now write into a real SQL server too.\ntools/oracle/driver-fetch/ is a small standalone Gradle project (not part of\nthe vendored source) that resolves the MariaDB Connector/J driver jar from\nMaven Central through the oracle's own GRADLE_USER_HOME - canonical upstream\ntooling, the jar itself gitignored and reproducible.\n\nTwo real findings, neither one a change to packages/engine's SQL storage\nport: MariaDB Connector/J does not parse jdbc:mariadb://user:password@host\nembedded userinfo the way this port's own mysql2 adapter does (upstream's\nown connection-properties config field is the documented fix, so the\nharness's generated config uses that instead); and an early draft of this\nharness raw-byte-diffed tileState/regionState against a separately-run\ncontrol render and reported false positives from those grids' real\nwall-clock timestamps, fixed by reusing the gate's own diffRenderState\ninstead of a second, less-tested comparison. No engine port code changed -\nthe SQL storage port was correct on its first genuine cross-engine test.\n\nROADMAP.md's Phase H section, docs/deviations.md's storage/sql section, and\nHANDOFF.md are updated with the full account, including what remains\nunproven (a Java-CLI-vs-TS-port cross-engine run specifically for SQLite or\nPostgreSQL, both already proven against real same-engine servers).\n\n呢個 issue 剩返嗰個未劃鉤嘅要求——java engine 寫嘅 sql storage,port 度讀唔讀到,\n反過嚟又得唔得——今次真係用一個真嘅 mariadb:11.4.7 docker container 兩個方向都\n證實咗。Java 寫嘅嘢,port 讀返嚟同 java 自己嘅 file storage 一模一樣(961 個\nhires tile、24 個 lowres tile、兩份 metadata、全部 render-state 決定性欄位都\n啱);port 寫嘅嘢,叫返 java 自己嘅 CLI 淨係開 webserver(冇 render 過,冇 map\nload 過)去讀,一樣位元一致噉讀返晒出嚟——用嘅仲係 java 自己嗰條正式讀 SQL\nstorage 嘅路,唔係測試專用嘅假嘢。搵到兩樣嘢,但都唔關 port 事:MariaDB\nConnector/J 唔識解「jdbc:mariadb://user:password@host」呢種寫法(改用\nconnection-properties 就得,唔使改 port);仲有第一版 harness 直接 byte-diff\nrender-state 撞板,因為嗰啲 timestamp 兩次 render 實會唔同,後尾改用返\ncompare.mjs 自己套 diffRenderState 就好返。Port 本身一隻字都冇改過。",
                category: "build",
                areas: ["build", "docs"],
                files: 8,
