                subject: "Close issue #31: modded textures.json parity, proven offline",
                details: "The last open half of Phase C's exit checks: textures-parity.mjs's\n--modded flag existed but had no legitimate pack to point at, and\nnothing wired it into the java side at all - it was accepted on the\ncommand line and then silently ignored. Closes it without a network\nconnection: tools/oracle/fixtures/syntheticModPack.mjs builds a small\nfully-synthetic resource pack in code (a new testmod: namespace, two\nblocks with real blockstate/model/texture chains, plus an override of\nminecraft:block/stone), the same \"generate it, never ship it\" approach\nvanillaShapedPack.ts already uses for its own fixture. --synthetic-modded\nmounts it as an extra, higher-priority pack root on both engines: the\njava side through its own packs/ folder (writeReferenceConfig now\nactually copies something there, and the render cache is keyed off the\npack's content hash so a regenerated fixture invalidates a stale\nreference), the ported side through render-ts.mjs's pre-existing\n--resource-pack flag, which had the right precedence and no caller\nuntil tsEngine.mjs learned to pass one through.\n\nVerified for real, not just wired: both engines produced 1725/1725\nmatching gallery entries (1723 vanilla + this pack's 2 new textures),\nand the harness decodes each of the pack's three texture keys on both\nsides and checks the actual pixel against the pack's own known colour\n- because \"the key exists\" proves nothing for the override case,\nminecraft:block/stone already exists in a plain vanilla render. All\nthree pixels matched exactly on both engines, including the override,\nwhich is the proof that the higher-priority pack root genuinely\nshadowed the vanilla jar rather than the vanilla texture quietly\nwinning underneath an unrelated pass.\n\nJudged against issue #31's own text - \"one modded pack\", not \"one\nreal downloaded mod\" - this closes the check the same way\nvanillaShapedPack.ts already stands in for a real client jar in its\nown tests: proving the code path (new-namespace discovery through the\natlas mechanism, a pack overriding a lower-priority root) rather than\nany one real mod's specific content. With check 2's render defect\nalready fixed (#46, closed) and check 3 already passing, issue #31\nitself is closed. ROADMAP.md's Phase C row moves to Done; HANDOFF.md\nrecords the full evidence including a manual pixel spot-check\nindependent of the harness's own assertion.\n\nPhase C exit checks, node tools/oracle/textures-parity.mjs\n--accept-download (vanilla, 1723/1723) and the same with\n--synthetic-modded (1725/1725) - both exit 0.\n\n執完 issue #31 最後一嚿骨:modded pack 嗰邊嘅 textures.json 對數,呢鑊唔使\n連一粒網絡封包都唔洗掟出去。冇合法嘅 modded pack 執到手,咁就自己整一個\n——testmod: 呢個全新 namespace,兩舊嘢連晒 blockstate、model、材質一條龍,\n仲加埋一個「翻叮」minecraft:block/stone 嘅材質,全部用 code 生成,一粒\nbytes 都唔使去 Mojang 攞。Java 嗰邊原來得個 flag 冇埋牙——講到明「呢個\nscript 仲未駁條線落 java 個 packs/ 資料夹」,而家真係駁埋佢,仲鎖埋個\ncache key 落個 pack 嘅內容度,唔會亂咁撞版本。TypeScript 嗰邊反而執少啲\n嘢,因為個 --resource-pack flag 本身已經企啱位,淨係冇人叫佢出嚟做嘢。\n\n驗證梗係要來真嘅:兩邊引擎跑出嚟 1725/1725 個 entry 對得晒,仲要逐粒像素\n解碼比對——因為 minecraft:block/stone 呢個 key 喺 vanilla render 都本身\n存在,單靠「有冇呢個 key」證明唔到「翻叮」真係生效咗,要真係解開張圖睇\n係咪嗰嚿自己整嘅顏色先算數。三個 key 嘅像素喺兩邊引擎度分毫不差,連\noverride 都啱晒。跟返 issue #31 自己嘅字面意思(「一個 modded pack」,\n唔係話一定要真係落載),同 vanillaShapedPack.ts 一直行緊嘅路一樣,考嗰啲\n真係要驗嘅 code path,唔係考某一個 mod 嘅獨門秘方。Check 2 嗰個 render bug\n(#46)同 check 3 都已經過咗,今次 issue #31 正式閂燈。",
