                subject: "CI: retry vitest's own RPC-heartbeat flake only, and fix a real dynamic-require crash the fix will now expose",
                details: "Two distinct, unrelated causes, both diagnosed against the real failing runs\nrather than guessed at.\n\n1. scripts/run-tests-ci.mjs (wired in as `pnpm test:ci`, called from ci.yml\n   in place of `pnpm test`). Silencing the vue-i18n warning flood (previous\n   commit) cut one CI run's log from ~50,000 lines to ~1,700 - a real, worthwhile\n   fix on its own - but the exact same \"[vitest-worker]: Timeout calling\n   \\\"onTaskUpdate\\\"\" error still fired on the very next push (run 30997969729,\n   commit e77f11a), with all 474 files still reported passed. vitest 3.2.7\n   hardcodes that RPC deadline at 60s (`DEFAULT_TIMEOUT` in its own bundled\n   chunk) with no config knob - not in vitest.config.ts, not in poolOptions, not\n   in an env var. It reproduces locally too, under load, alongside ordinary\n   30s/120s test timeouts in unrelated real-I/O tests (real SQLite, a real CLI\n   e2e server, a real vue-tsc subprocess) - this is CI-runner contention, not a\n   defect in any test. The wrapper runs the real `vitest run` and retries a\n   clean attempt only when the summary shows zero failed files, zero failed\n   tests, and that one RPC-timeout error - never when a real test or file is\n   reported failed. Verified against both shapes locally: a run with genuine\n   test failures was correctly propagated without a retry attempt, and the\n   detection regexes were checked against captured vitest summary output with\n   ANSI codes stripped.\n\n2. packages/app/build.mjs. While confirming an unrelated lead about\n   packages/app's esbuild bundle, reproduced a real, separate, currently-\n   invisible bug: esbuild's `format: \"esm\"` output for the main process leaves\n   a bundled CommonJS dependency's `require(\"util\")` (and any other Node\n   builtin) as a call through esbuild's own `__require` runtime shim, which is\n   `typeof require !== \"undefined\" ? require : throw`. A plain Node ESM module\n   has no global `require` at all, so the shim throws \"Dynamic require of\n   \\\"util\\\" is not supported\" the instant such a call runs. pngjs - reached\n   transitively through the render pipeline on essentially every texture -\n   requires `util` unconditionally at the top of its own entry module, before\n   any PNG operation runs. Reproduced directly: bundling a two-line pngjs\n   smoke test with build.mjs's exact esbuild options throws that exact error;\n   adding a `createRequire(import.meta.url)` banner so the bundle has its own\n   real `require` fixes it, verified against a real pngjs encode. This has\n   never shown up in CI because the job that would run the packaged app\n   (`package`/Windows installer) is gated behind `check` succeeding, and\n   `check` has been failing at the test step for the unrelated reason above on\n   every push for a long stretch - so fixed it now, before fix (1) lets\n   `check` finally pass and unblocks that job for the first time.\n\nExternalizing pngjs, rather than fixing the require, would have been the\nwrong shape of fix: electron-builder.config.cjs explicitly ships `dist/**/*`\nand excludes `node_modules` - the whole design is a self-contained bundle\nwith nothing on disk to resolve an external import against at packaged-app\nruntime.\n\nCI 一直死喺同一句說話, 呢排先聽出嚟係邊句: 全部 test file 都話自己過咗,\n然後最尾先嚟一句\"心跳都聽唔到\", 好似個裁判判完全場都話冇事然後先話犯規。\n仲有個瞓咗好耐嘅炸彈, 挖深啲先發現: 個 app 一開機用個貼圖, 就會撞正一個\n\"呢度冇 require 呢樣嘢\" 嘅坑, 不過個坑喺呢排根本冇人行過, 因為前面嗰句\n\"心跳唔到\"已經攔咗成條隊。而家兩個一齊拆, 好過拆咗第一個先俾第二個嚇一跳。",
                category: "build",
                areas: ["build", "shell"],
                files: 4,
