                subject: "Remove WebServer: nothing ever asked the engine to run one twice",
                details: "WebServer (runtime/webserver.ts) spawned the upstream engine a second\ntime with -w and refused to report a URL until it had actually opened\na TCP connection to prove the bind worked. Thorough, well tested (7\ntests), and dead: no orchestrator, local, Docker or remote, ever\nplanned a launch with role \"web-server\". The class had been standing\nin an empty room since the commit that built it, waiting for a caller\nwho was never coming, because LocalMapHandler already serves every\nrender this app produces - straight off disk, no second JVM required.\n\nRemoved the class and its test, updated the runtime barrel and\ndocker-and-local.md's \"web server\" section to describe what actually\nruns, and recorded the decision as D19 in design/docs/decisions.md.\nThe RuntimeRole \"web-server\" launch-planning code stays in plan.ts,\ntyped and tested, in case a live upstream server is ever genuinely\nneeded; it just does not get to keep an unused class around while it\nwaits.\n\n原來個 WebServer 喺度苦等一個永遠唔會嚟嘅來電,足足等咗一個 commit 咁耐 —\n成個 class 起晒引擎、寫晒 webserver.conf、仲要真係開條 TCP 線去確認個\nport 有冇聽緊先肯報 URL,結果由頭到尾冇一個 orchestrator 肯用佢嗌\n\"web-server\" 呢個 role。原因好簡單:LocalMapHandler 直接喺硬盤度讀\nrender 完嘅嘢畀睇,邊使多開一個 JVM 嚟做多餘工。今次幫呢個 class 執骨,\n連測試一齊移除,喺 docker-and-local.md 同 decisions.md(D19)寫低點解\n——起碼佢走得明明白白,唔使當幽靈咁飄喺個 repo 度。",
