                subject: "Make the vendor cross-checks loud, and stop grading a stale config build",
                details: "Two silent traps in packages/config's test suite, both invisible in a\ngreen run.\n\nschema.test.ts and controlPolicy.test.ts each carried their own\ndescribe.skipIf(!vendorAvailable)(...), which quietly skips every\ncross-check against the vendored BlueMap Java the moment the submodule is\nmissing - which it always is in CI today, since ci.yml's checkout step\ndeliberately does not fetch it. A skipped describe block reads identically\nto a passing one in a scrolled-past CI log. Extracted the whole mechanism\ninto a new shared vendorGate.ts: vendorSuffix now names the skip reason\ndirectly in the describe block's own title, so it survives being read out\nof a log with nothing else to go on, and requireVendorInCi() registers a\nreal assertion that only fails - loudly, by name - once CI actually sets\nMBM_VENDOR_REQUIRED=1, which nothing does yet. That is deliberate: turning\ntoday's silent skip into today's hard failure would redden a workflow this\ntask was told not to touch. The one line that would light this up for real\nis recorded below rather than added.\n\nSeparately, configExplainCoverage.test.ts imports @material-bluemap/config\nby specifier, which resolves through its package.json \"main\" to a\ngit-ignored dist/ that only pnpm --filter @material-bluemap/config run\nbuild ever refreshes. Editing mask.ts's doc text an hour ago and running\nthis suite without rebuilding produced a green pass against the previous\nschema - confirmed by hand: the new guard immediately caught that exact\nstale dist/ before this commit's own build brought it current. Added\nconfigPackageFreshness.ts, the same newest-mtime-wins walk\npackages/app/test/freshBundle.ts already uses for the screenshot harness,\nnow proven against disposable temp directories rather than against this\nrepository's own build state.\n\nThe workflow line CI needs, not added here because .github is another\nagent's: ci.yml's \"check\" job checkout step (design/packages, \"Lint,\nbuild, test\") needs `submodules: true` added to its actions/checkout@v4,\nand its own comment there - \"the vendored BlueMap submodule ... is\ndeliberately not checked out\" - is now inaccurate and worth a line saying\nwhy once someone owns that file again. Once fetched, adding `env:\nMBM_VENDOR_REQUIRED: \"1\"` to the pnpm test step turns a missing submodule\nfrom a named skip into a real CI failure.\n\nNeither trap was a bug in what was being asserted - both were bugs in\nwhether the assertion ever got to run at all, which a passing suite\ncannot tell you about itself.\n\n粵語：packages/config 個 test suite 有兩個靜雞雞嘅陷阱,行綠咗都睇唔出。\n\nschema.test.ts 同 controlPolicy.test.ts 各自有個\ndescribe.skipIf(!vendorAvailable),vendor 個 submodule 一冇喺度就靜雞雞\nskip 晒啲 cross-check——而而家 CI 一路都冇呢個 submodule,因為 ci.yml 個\ncheckout step 專登冇 fetch 佢。Skip 咗嘅 describe block 喺 CI log 度睇落\n同 pass 咗一模一樣。而家抽咗做一個共用嘅 vendorGate.ts:vendorSuffix 會將\nskip 嘅原因直接寫入 describe 個名度,requireVendorInCi() 會登記一個真係\n會 fail 嘅斷言——但淨係喺 CI 真係set 咗 MBM_VENDOR_REQUIRED=1 先會爆,而\n而家冇人set。呢個係刻意嘅:如果而家就將靜默 skip 變爆炸,會整爆一個呢次\n任務叫我唔好郁嘅 workflow。真正要加嘅嗰一行,寫喺低面,冇直接加落去。\n\n另外,configExplainCoverage.test.ts 引用 @material-bluemap/config 呢個\npackage,實際上係經佢個 package.json 嘅 \"main\" 指去一個冇入 git 嘅\ndist/,淨係 pnpm --filter @material-bluemap/config run build 先會更新。\n一個鐘頭前改咗 mask.ts 段文件,冇 rebuild 就跑呢個 suite,真係俾佢 pass\n咗——用返舊 schema pass 嘅。加咗個新 guard 之後即刻捉到嗰個真係過時嘅\ndist/,呢個 commit 自己 build 完先變返綠。呢個新加嘅\nconfigPackageFreshness.ts,同 packages/app/test/freshBundle.ts 幫個\nscreenshot harness 用嘅「揾最新 mtime」邏輯一樣,而家用臨時資料夾實測過。\n\nCI 缺嗰一行(冇喺度加,因為 .github 而家係第二個 agent 睇住):ci.yml 個\n\"check\" job(\"Lint, build, test\")嘅 checkout step 要加\n`submodules: true`,佢原本個 comment 話「submodule 專登冇 checkout」而\n家已經講錯咗,要有人執返呢個檔案先改得。跟住 pnpm test 嗰步加\n`env: MBM_VENDOR_REQUIRED: \"1\"`,就可以由「靜默 skip」變返做真係會爆嘅\nCI failure。\n\n呢兩個窿都唔係斷言本身錯——係斷言有冇真係跑過呢件事,一個 pass 咗嘅\nsuite 係唔會自己講畀你知嘅。",
