                subject: "test+docs: prove the head-of-queue race is safe, drop #40 from ROADMAP's gap list",
                details: "Adds one more MapUpdateService test: a region already at the head of\nRenderManager's queue (i.e. currently being worked on) gets a second, equal\ntask queued *behind* it when a new watch event arrives, rather than being\nrefused as a duplicate or racing the running one. This is RenderManager\n.scheduleRenderTask's own containsRenderTask behaviour - it deliberately\nexempts index 0 - verified directly against the real queue instead of taken on\nfaith, closing the second of the issue's own \"two hard parts\" checklist items.\n\nROADMAP.md: moves \"Watch-driven re-render\" from Phase E's \"not ported\" list to\na dated \"Ported on 2026-08-05 (issue #40)\" entry, matching the file's existing\nconvention for #41/#29, and states plainly what still isn't done - the\npackages/cli hookup, left alone because that package was mid-restructure by a\ndifferent task in the same pass.\n\nRefs #40.\n\n一句講晒:證多一鑊 - 個 region 啱啱先起緊工,新一單嘢嚟到唔會打尖\n爭崩頭,老老實實排喺後面等,唔會兩份工同時间撞埋一齊整污糟塊地。\nROADMAP 都執返靚,#40 呢單嘢正式由「未做」榜移咗去「做咗」嗰邊。",
