                details: "Two housekeeping items the server-porting agent flagged about its own work,\npicked up before starting the CLI: docs/deviations.md had no entry for the\n/maps/{id}/update trigger route or the res.flushHeaders() SSE fix, and issue\n#29's checklist asked for a render-driver test against a real\npackages/worldgen world through a real ResourcePack, not the structural fake\nWorld the existing test used. Both are now true: a new \"Server package\"\nsection in deviations.md documents the route and the flush fix, and\nrender-driver.test.ts gained a test that loads a real MCAWorld-parsed anvil\nworld, meshes it against a small self-authored (Mojang-free) ResourcePack,\nand asserts real hires tiles landed in a real FileMapStorage. The old\nfake-World test stays untouched — nothing here got weaker, only more proven.\n\n兩單手尾,喺開手整 CLI 之前先執: docs/deviations.md 一直冇記低\n/maps/{id}/update 呢條觸發路由，同埋修 SSE 嗰個 res.flushHeaders()；issue\n#29 張清單又話要用真.worldgen 世界、真 ResourcePack 去測 RenderDriver，\n唔可以淨係用假嘅 World 交功課。而家兩樣都補返晒:deviations.md 新增\n「Server package」一節記低條路由同個 flush 修復,render-driver.test.ts\n就加咗個測試,真係用 MCAWorld 讀一個生成嘅 anvil 世界、配一個自己寫、\n同 Mojang 冇關嘅細 ResourcePack 去 render,驗到真係有 hires tile 寫入\n真正嘅 FileMapStorage。舊嗰個假 World 測試原封不動——冇拆冇減，淨係加多咗證據。",
