                subject: "Register the last unwired copy surfaces and fix a genuine tab-group-picker search leak",
                details: "Nine copy-catalogue surfaces (accounts, configExplain, docsViewer, menuSearch,\nnotificationsBulk, panels, presets, speed, tabGroupPicker) sat written but\nunplugged, so their strings rendered English at every funny level and in every\nlanguage. Registered them into surfaces/index.ts, folded the leftover\nUpdateStatusRow staging copy (uiFixes.ts) into settings.ts where it belongs, and\nthen chased the fallout: two dynamic-key t() calls that no scanner could ever\nfind (SpeedControl.vue, DockedSurface.vue) rewritten as literal per-value\nlookups, a missing config.search.badPattern sibling entry, a case-broken FACTS\npin in docsViewer.lede, and a stray em-dash in backup.whyNotLfs. GitHubAccountsList\nand NoticeBulkToolbar had catalogue entries nobody called; wired refresh/switch\nfeedback and dismiss/export previews into the real UI rather than deleting the\nunused keys.\n\nAlso found and fixed the bug a throwaway repro test was written to confirm:\nTabStrip keeps one TabGroupPicker instance alive behind a v-menu, so a search\ntyped while moving one tab used to still be filtering the list next time any\ntab's picker opened. focus() -- the one call the host already makes on every\nopen -- now clears query/regexMode/flags too, with a permanent regression test\nreplacing the \"delete after use\" repro. Separately, TabGroupPicker's own\ndocument-level Tab trap could double-handle a boundary press that Vuetify's\nv-menu had already resolved correctly, walking a correctly-returned focus one\nplace too far backward; it now no-ops once focus has already left the popover.\n\nOne assertion in tabGroupPickerMount.test.ts is left honestly red: it passes\nalone and passes as part of a filtered run, but lands focus on the wrong button\nonly when the full 19-test file runs together, and the exact wrong target\nvaries by which other tests ran first. Documented in place with what was ruled\nout rather than weakened to pass.\n\n九個寫低咗但冇接電嘅字典 surface（accounts、configExplain、docsViewer、\nmenuSearch、notificationsBulk、panels、presets、speed、tabGroupPicker）今次\n全部駁返落 surfaces/index.ts，所有語言、所有搞笑等級終於講返人話，唔使再\n死頂英文。仲執埋兩個掃描器見唔到嘅動態 key t() call（靠模板字串砌出嚟嗰\n種）、一個漏咗嘅 config.search.badPattern、一個俾大階字母累到冧咗嘅 FACTS\npin，同埋 backup.ts 入面一劃走犯嘅破折號。\n\n仲順手捉埋一個「用完即棄」嘅 repro test 想證明嘅漏洞：TabStrip 成程式淨係\n留住一個 TabGroupPicker 實例喺 v-menu 後面，所以搜尋過一個分頁之後，個\nsearch box 嘅字會賴死唔走，落到第二個分頁都仲喺度篩緊。而家 focus() 每次\n開返都會清埋佢，仲加咗個永久 regression test 頂替嗰個「用完就刪」嘅 repro。\n另外 TabGroupPicker 自己個 document 層級嘅 Tab trap 會同 Vuetify v-menu\n自己嗰套撞埋一齊處理同一次揿掣，將啱啱先啱返嘅 focus 屈多一步行錯咗地方，\n而家一見到 focus 已經走出咗個 popover 就即刻縮手唔理。\n\ntabGroupPickerMount.test.ts 留低一條斷言老實噉紅住：單獨行得過，篩住行都\n得，但成個十九條 test 齊齊行嗰陣就會揸錯掣，仲要揸邊個掣都睇住邊班 test\n行先。就地寫低查過乜嘢、剩返乜嘢未解，冇靠削弱斷言呃過去。",
