                subject: "server: live/sse, live/players.json, live/markers.json with honest empty stubs",
                details: "Ports SseConnection/SseConnectionManager (a bounded per-connection queue,\ndrop-and-close on a stuck client, a has-connections transition) and\nLiveDataSupplierBroadcaster (poll-while-someone-is-listening, notify on\nchange) from MapRequestHandler/SseConnectionManager/LiveDataSupplierBroadcaster.\nA mounted map always has a live-data supplier now: real ones may be passed in,\nand otherwise it gets upstream's own JSON shape for zero online players\n({\"players\":[]}) and zero marker sets ({}) instead of 404ing an endpoint the\nviewer expects to be able to poll — never invented data, just upstream's\nactual answer for nothing to report. live/sse, live/players.json and\nlive/markers.json now take priority over MapStorageHandler's raw-storage\nfallback, exactly mirroring MapRequestHandler's registration order.\n\nAlso fixes a real bug the new tests caught before anyone else could: Node\nbuffers HTTP response headers until the first write, and nothing was forcing\na flush on connect, so any live/sse client past the first (the first got\nlucky off the default suppliers' initial broadcast) hung forever waiting for\nheaders that were never sent. res.flushHeaders() on open() now gives every\nconnection what upstream's transport gives for free.\n\n8 new tests cover the exact lifecycle #41 calls out: connecting, several\nclients receiving one broadcast identically, a client disappearing without a\ngoodbye, and every connection closing when its map is unmounted — plus the\nstub contract, the override path, and SSE staying off when configured off\nwhile the JSON endpoints keep answering.\n\nRefs #41.\n\n一句講晒:即時資料嗰截,連埋 SSE 一齊搬咗嚟。冇玩家上線?\n唔使裝\"搵唔到\",老老實實答返個上游都會答嘅「一個玩家都冇」\n—— `{\"players\":[]}`,唔係老作。仲喺度順手拆咗個伏:淨係\n`writeHead` 唔 `write` 唔 `flushHeaders`,Node 會扣住個 header\n唔放,第二個接嘅客一係等到天荒地老。而家開線果下即刻\nflush,唔使等邊個啱啱好廣播咗嘢先至冧巴一送。",
                category: "services",
                areas: ["services"],
                files: 7,
