                subject: "server: port MapStorageRequestHandler for real tiles/settings/textures/assets over HTTP",
                details: "Adds MapStorageHandler, mounted at /maps/{id}/... alongside the existing\nStaticHandler/RemoteProxyHandler/LocalMapHandler siblings. It serves hires and\nlowres tiles, settings.json, textures.json and assets/* straight out of a real\nMapStorage (FileMapStorage today), porting MapStorageRequestHandler's tile\nregex, its meta-data switch and writeToResponse's exact content-negotiation\nbyte for byte: gzip passthrough when the client already accepts the stored\ncompression, on-the-fly gzip otherwise (never for PNG), 204 for a tile that\nwas never rendered, 404 for anything else. 14 new route-level tests exercise\nit against a real FileMapStorage, including the gotcha that undici's fetch()\nquietly auto-negotiates and re-decompresses gzip bodies out from under a\nnaive test — those assertions go over a raw http.request instead so the wire\nbytes are what gets checked.\n\nRefs #41.\n\n一句講晒:上游個 web server 識畀 tile,我哋而家都識喇 —\n四個檔加埋一個新阿豬阿狗,專門負責由真身 MapStorage 度攞嘢出嚟,\ngzip 唔 gzip 都跟上游套邏輯,一個字唔改。仲要拆穿咗 fetch() 呢個\n「幫你自動解壓仲唔話你知」嘅老千,啲 test 改用原始 http.request\n先至照到實際線路上嘅 bytes,唔係俾佢呃咗都仲以為自己啱。",
