                details: "Turns out packages/ui's typecheck never got past TabGroupPicker.vue's parse\nerror to actually look at the rest of the project. With that fixed, vue-tsc\nfinally reached a dozen more real findings scattered across unrelated files\n-- the swept commit's ~9 lanes never got a chance to see each other's damage:\n\n- ciRenders.test.ts: four `let resolveX = null` variables assigned only\n  inside a Promise executor, then read with `?.()` in the outer scope.\n  TypeScript's control-flow analysis does not cross that function boundary,\n  so it kept treating each one as narrowed to its `null` initialiser and\n  flagged the read as calling `never`. Boxed each in a `{ current }` ref,\n  which sidesteps the limitation entirely.\n- CiRenderScreen.test.ts: an `it.each` table's three answer objects lost\n  their literal `status` field to widening once combined into one array,\n  so none of them satisfied CiRepositoryNameAvailability's discriminated\n  union any more. Cast per row.\n- SpeedControl.test.ts: a destructuring cast one array level too deep --\n  `[unknown, unknown][][]` instead of a fixed two-tuple -- meant\n  `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` added `| undefined` to what should have been\n  a definite pair.\n- PathField.vue: `error-messages` and `density` were being fed `?? undefined`\n  and a bare possibly-undefined prop respectively, both illegal once\n  exactOptionalPropertyTypes stops treating \"explicitly undefined\" the same\n  as \"not passed\"; both components' real prop types take `null`.\n- projectModel.ts: the same exactOptionalPropertyTypes rule caught passing\n  a genuinely-optional `separator` straight through; spread it in only when\n  actually set, exactly like the sibling storage call three lines up.\n- AppSettings.vue / .test.ts: `settingsSections.ts` had grown an \"updates\"\n  entry with nowhere to render -- an unfinished lane, not a typo, since\n  UpdateStatusRow.vue and useUpdates.ts already existed fully built and\n  tested and simply were never wired into the settings tab strip. Wired it\n  the way components/update/index.ts's own doc comment already prescribes:\n  App.vue's one shared `createUpdates()` now also reaches this row, so the\n  banner and the settings tab can never disagree about what is staged.\n\n即係話,個 parse bug 一日未執,vue-tsc 就一日睇唔到後面嗰九條友各自留低嘅手尾 -\n四條喺 Promise executor 入面先至有得着值嘅變數、一個宽咗做 string 嘅 status\n字段、一個多咗一層 array 嘅 destructuring、两个 exactOptionalPropertyTypes\n中招嘅 prop,仲有一個得個名冇個實嘅 Updates tab。而家全部拆解晒,靓仔到不得了。",
