                subject: "Offer to host a CI-rendered map on Pages, and make the map survive the trip",
                details: "Two halves of the same gap.\n\nThe workflow already had an `artifact-and-pages` output wired end to end, and no\nscreen in the application ever set it -- a finished feature nobody could reach.\nThe CI render screen now offers it, off by default, because rendering a world is\na private act until somebody says otherwise, and it says the two things a person\nwould otherwise discover afterwards: the map lands under the documentation site\nat /map/ rather than on top of it, and a world too large to assemble on one\nrunner ships in parts, which cannot be hosted this way at all.\n\nThe other half is that the published map would not have worked. Pages serves the\nfiles that exist under the names they have; the engine writes `0.prbm.gz` and the\nviewer asks for `0.prbm`. BlueMap's own server bridges that gap and so does this\napp's -- Pages does not, so every tile would have 404'd and the run would have\ngone green with a working link to an empty sky. The merge job now runs the new\n`static-host` command over the copy bound for Pages, which flips the flag, checks\nit against the files really on disk, writes .nojekyll, and exits non-zero rather\nthan publishing a site nobody can use. The downloadable artifact is uploaded\nbefore that step and is untouched.\n\nVerified by running the built CLI: exit 0 on a good map with the flag flipped and\n.nojekyll written, exit 1 on a map whose textures were never gzipped.\n\n兩件事其實係同一個窿。個 workflow 一早做好咗上 Pages 嘅路,但成個 app 冇一個掣\n撳得到 -- 等於整好咗間房冇開門。而家開咗門,預設熄機,仲會事先講明幅圖擺喺\n/map/ 唔會踩低份文件,同埋太大嘅世界要拆件送,拆咗件就上唔到。\n第二件更加陰功:唔理佢嘅話,發佈完每一塊 tile 都會 404,個 run 仲要係綠色,\nlink 撳得開,入面一片藍天。而家出發之前會夾正個掣先,唔妥就唔好去。",
                category: "interface",
                areas: ["interface"],
