                details: "Shard planning now spends the available jobs on real render work instead of proudly meeting the deadline with six enormous slices while the rest of the runner queue watches. A fixed setup-cost model keeps parallelism useful without turning every job into an installation marathon, and the Bedrock notes now mark the remaining proof boundary plainly.\\n\\nRender shard 而家會用多啲有用嘅平行火力，唔再用六件超大切件扮係準時就算，等其他 runner 喺旁邊食花生。固定 setup 成本會防止切到每件只係搬檔案，Bedrock 文件亦老實寫返仲欠嘅真機驗證。",
