        version: "0.1.0-build.117",
        tag: "v0.1.0-build.117",
        date: "2026-08-04T00:04:51-04:00",
        commit: "7a568277270903c18ff7a92c1e55d8c9d74fa3a6",
        entries: [
            {
                sha: "7a568277270903c18ff7a92c1e55d8c9d74fa3a6",
                shortSha: "7a56827727",
                date: "2026-08-04T00:04:51-04:00",
                subject: "Compare the gallery on the pictures, and the Phase D gate passes",
                details: "The last file standing was textures.json, and its first difference was\nthe base64 PNG in entry zero. Decoded, the picture is identical. So are\nthe other 2091: same width, same height, same pixel for every sample.\nThe two documents agree on the entry count, the order, every id and\nevery colour; what differs is that ImageIO packs a small-palette\ntexture into an indexed PNG at one, two or four bits per pixel while\nthis project's encoder writes eight-bit RGBA. Five hundred and\nthirty-two of the 2092 are that shape.\n\nThat is decision D3 - PNG parity on decoded pixels, never bytes -\narriving through a different door, so it gets the same answer. The\ngallery is now compared by value on every field except the image, and\nthe image on decoded pixels, with a re-encode counted and printed\nrather than folded away. Proving it required teaching the harness's\nPNG reader the sub-eight-bit depths, because refusing to decode a\nquarter of the gallery and calling the rest a match is precisely the\n\"could not check\" that reads as agreement.\n\nFour checks added to the selftest, since this excuses an encoder and\nmust therefore be shown biting on the picture: the same image written\ntwo ways is a re-encode, a single changed pixel is a divergence naming\nits coordinates, and an image that cannot be decoded is reported rather\nthan accepted.\n\nThe gate on the 200x200 fixture now exits 0. RESULT: identical, 63\nfiles matched, every hires tile byte for byte after decompression,\nevery lowres tile pixel for pixel. The mesher agrees with the engine it\nreplaces. A 1000x1000 run on a different seed is under way and this\ncommit claims nothing about it.\n\n---\n\n最後一個唔啱嘅檔係 textures.json,第一個差異喺第零個 entry 張 PNG。\n解碼開嚟睇?一模一樣。其餘 2091 張都係。兩份文件個數目、次序、每個\nid、每隻顏色全部夾晒;唯一分別係 ImageIO 見到色少就索性用 1/2/4 bit\n嘅索引 PNG,而我哋隻 encoder 一律寫 8-bit RGBA - 2092 張入面有 532\n張係咁。\n\n即係 D3 嗰單嘢(PNG 睇像素唔睇 byte)換咗道門入嚟,咁就同一個答案。\n不過要證明到,就要教識個 PNG reader 讀 sub-8-bit - 唔係嘅話四份一\n個 gallery 「睇唔到」,而「睇唔到」讀落就係「冇問題」,正正係呢個\nharness 存在嘅原因。\n\n個閘而家 exit 0。RESULT: identical,63 個檔全對,每張 hires tile 解\n壓之後 byte 對 byte,每張 lowres tile 粒粒像素對。隻 mesher 同佢要\n取代嘅引擎,講返同一句嘢。1000x1000 嗰鋪跑緊,呢個 commit 唔會替佢\n講嘢。",
                category: "build",
                areas: ["build"],
                files: 4,
            }
        ],
