                subject: "Float the control bar below the title bar it was sitting on",
                details: "The first green run's own captures showed it: the viewer's floating\ncontrol bar was anchored at top: 0, which was correct for a browser\ntab and wrong for the desktop build, where the window now draws its\nown Material title bar in that exact strip. The menu button covered\nthe logo and most of the title, and the top-right cluster parked\nitself precisely on minimize, maximize and close - three buttons that\nrender, work, and could not be seen or clicked under a pill that\narrived later and sat on top.\n\nAppTitleBar already publishes --mb-titlebar-height for exactly this,\nand #map-container already consumes it; the control bar now reads the\nsame property, so it starts under the chrome on desktop and keeps the\nfull viewport in a browser, where the property is never set.\n\nAlso carried here: @fontsource/roboto-mono enters the ui package's\ndependencies (the import lands with the wave in flight), so the\nlockfile change travels with the decision that caused it.\n\n---\n\n睇返自己張截圖先發現：個浮動控制列釘死喺 top: 0，喺瀏覽器啱晒，\n但桌面版而家嗰條位置係人哋自己畫嘅 Material title bar。個 menu 掣\n坐咗喺個 logo 同標題度，右上角成串掣仲要唔偏唔倚壓正喺最小化、\n最大化同關閉三兄弟上面 - 三個掣又真又работ，就係俾人坐住睇唔到\n撳唔到。\n\nAppTitleBar 一早為咗呢件事出咗 --mb-titlebar-height，#map-container\n一早識用；而家控制列都讀埋呢個數，桌面版乖乖哋喺 chrome 下面開工，\n瀏覽器版繼續霸全屏 - 各得其所。",
